e 'test_bump_recall' verifies updating recall count in pg_episodic_store","Uses unittest.mock.patch to mock get_memories and update_memory","Validates that bump_recall increments recall_count from '0' to '1' in metadata"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8ivh7_b33f1b6e2197","importance":2,"narrative":"The user inspected a specific test case in the episodic store test suite. This test ensures that calling bump_recall correctly updates the memory metadata's recall count.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Inspecting unit test for bump_recall functionality","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:39.832Z","title":"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8j07o_2f7ee78a0ba0":{"observation":{"concepts":["vector database upsert","similarity threshold","vector search filtering","embedding management"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The `create_memory` function performs an upsert into a collection with metadata and embeddings.","`create_unique_memory` checks for existing similar memories using a similarity threshold (default 0.95) before creating a new entry.","The `search_memory` function supports distance-based filtering (min/max distance) and metadata filtering (e.g., 'novel' flag).","Similarity is calculated using distance (max_distance = 1.0 - similarity)."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8j07o_2f7ee78a0ba0","importance":4,"narrative":"The user inspected the implementation of the memory management system to understand how memories are created, searched, and deduplicated based on similarity thresholds.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Code review of memory creation and search logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:45.971Z","title":"Inspecting agentmemory/main.py implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8j2md_9f24b07f4f39":{"observation":{"concepts":["python package inspection","function signature discovery"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Function `get_memory(category, id, include_embeddings=True)` exists at line 189 of .venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"files":[".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8j2md_9f24b07f4f39","importance":3,"narrative":"The user executed a grep command to locate the exact definition and line number of the `get_memory` function within the installed `agentmemory` package.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Locating function definition in site-packages","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:49.091Z","title":"Search for get_memory definition in agentmemory","type":"command_run"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8j4xk_32bff05d7f95":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory retrieval","vector database collections","embedding retrieval"],"confidence":1,"facts":["get_memory(category, id, include_embeddings=True) retrieves specific memory by ID within a category.","Uses get_client().get_or_create_collection(category) to access the relevant collection.","Retrieval logic depends on get_include_types to determine if embeddings are fetched."],"files":[".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8j4xk_32bff05d7f95","importance":3,"narrative":"Inspected the source code for the get_memory function to understand how the memory retrieval process handles category selection and embedding inclusion. This is critical for understanding the underlying data retrieval mechanism in the agent's memory system.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Reviewing memory retrieval logic in agentmemory/main.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:52.086Z","title":"Inspect get_memory implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8j7b6_9e20bbf05aee":{"observation":{"concepts":["memory retrieval logic","ChromaDB integration","vector database querying"],"confidence":1,"facts":["The get_memory function retrieves specific memory IDs from a collection.","Uses chroma_collection_to_list to process results.","Includes logging for successful and failed memory retrieval attempts.","Returns the first memory object if found, or None if the list is empty."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8j7b6_9e20bbf05aee","importance":3,"narrative":"The user inspected the implementation details of the memory retrieval function within the agentmemory package. This reveals the logic used to fetch and validate individual memory entries from the vector database.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Reading lines 210-225 of the memory retrieval logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:55.168Z","title":"Inspect agentmemory/main.py implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8jajc_192f1764b719":{"observation":{"concepts":["episodic memory","memory retrieval"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["Modified /Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py","Added 'get_memory' to the import list from 'agentmemory'"],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8jajc_192f1764b719","importance":5,"narrative":"Updated the imports in the episodic memory storage module to include the get_memory function. This allows the module to retrieve single memory entries in addition to existing search and list capabilities.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Added get_memory import to pg_episodic_store.py","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:58:59.350Z","title":"Update imports in pg_episodic_store.py","type":"file_edit"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8jd50_2e7ba04544df":{"observation":{"concepts":["python package exports","module initialization"],"confidence":0.9,"facts":["The string \"get_memory\" exists in .venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/__init__.py"],"files":[".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/__init__.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8jd50_2e7ba04544df","importance":3