teLLM","input injection guarding","structured prompt engineering"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Uses LiteLLM for intent classification into QUERY, DECISION, EXECution, and ESCALATION.","Implements a rule-based pre-filter stage before LLM processing.","Includes security scanning via xnch.security.injection_guard.","Defines a JSON schema for structured intent extraction including action_type, entity_class, and urgency."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588","importance":5,"narrative":"Inspected the core intent classification module to understand how user inputs are parsed, validated for injections, and categorized into actionable intents. This is a critical component of the pipeline's decision-making logic.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Analyzing LiteLLM-backed intent classification logic","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:59:54.185Z","title":"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation","type":"file_read"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b":{"observation":{"concepts":["intent classification","pytest fixture","mocking async clients","unit testing pipeline"],"confidence":1,"facts":["Tests cover IntentClass types: EXECUTION, QUERY, and ESCALATION.","Uses pytest and unittest.mock to simulate LiteLLM responses.","Includes tests for handling ambiguous inputs that trigger ClarificationRequired exceptions.","Mocks httpx.AsyncClient to control LLM response simulation."],"files":["/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py"],"id":"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b","importance":3,"narrative":"Read the test suite for the intent interpreter to understand how the system handles different intent classifications and ambiguity levels. This provides context for the expected behavior of the LLM-driven intent parsing logic.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Examining unit tests for the IntentInterpreter pipeline component","timestamp":"2026-06-26T17:5