rtance":3,"narrative":"Performed a directory listing of the .opencode/agents/ path to understand the organizational structure of the agent system. This identifies the key modules available for the AI agent to interact with.","sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","subtitle":"Exploration of agent configuration and structure","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:06.099Z","title":"Directory listing of .opencode/agents/","type":"discovery"},"type":"compressed"},"obs_mqv8ower_5e0f5b9074c2":{"observation":{"hookType":"reasoning","id":"obs_mqv8ower_5e0f5b9074c2","raw":{"messageID":"msg_f051984f9001UMDqXzHV2UNHcA","text":"Now I understand the layout of `.opencode/agents/`. These are the subagent types I can use as part of the `task` tool system. The available agent types include:\n\n- `devtools/code-reviewer` - Code review\n- `devtools/debugger` - Debugging\n- `devtools/refactoring-specialist` - Code refactoring\n- `devtools/test-automator` - Tests\n- `devtools/legacy-modernizer` - Legacy code modernization\n- `devtools/performance-engineer` - Performance\n- `devops/docker-specialist` - Docker\n- `devops/kubernetes-specialist` - K8s\n- `languages/python-pro` - Python specialist\n- `ai/llm-architect` - LLM systems\n- `ai/ml-engineer` - ML engineering\n- etc.\n\nBut these are the subagent types from the `task` tool, not the `.opencode/agents/` directory. The `.opencode/agents/` directory seems to mirror the same agent types. Let me check what's inside a few of these directories to understand the format.\n\nActually, these are simply the available subagent types for the `task` tool. The `.opencode/agents/` directory is the local cache of these agent definitions.\n\nLet me create a todo list and start spinning agents for each fix. I'll batch the independent fixes into parallel agents.\n\nHere's my plan:\n\n**Critical fixes (8):**\n1. `proactivity/engine.py` — wrong method + non-existent tables + port mismatch\n2. `nexi/main.py` — no-op URL replace\n3. `xnch/main.py` — APScheduler lambda\n4. `pg_episodic_store.py` — UUID-zero + retrieve_similar ignores query_text\n5. `vision_encoder.py` — wrong PIL import + wrong moondream method\n6. `graph_store.py` — sync dual-write + duplicate relations\n\n**High fixes (10):**\n7. `score_adapter.py` — context_json column\n8. `context_assembler.py` — bump_recall never called\n9. `nexi_gateway.py` — user turn after LLM + entity ID + private _redis access\n10. `voice_daemon.py` — int16→float32\n11. `langfuse_client.py` — sync httpx\n12. `graph_extractor.py` — GraphStore without relationship_store\n\n**Medium fixes (6):**\n13. `intent_interpreter.py` — entity extraction\n14. `memory_guard.py` — never called\n15. `trust_model.py` — hasattr scan\n16. `cold_start_seeder.py` — full scan\n17. `attention_filter.py` — create_task from sync\n\n**Low fixes (5):**\n18. `injection_guard.py` — lookahead case\n19. `nexi_gateway.py` — fire-and-forget (combined with #9)\n20. Dockerfile — python version + .dockerignore\n21. K8s manifests — secret injection\n22. `voice_daemon.py` — language detection\n\nSince the user wants to \"spin agents from .opencode/agents/\", they want me to use the task tool with appropriate subagent types. Let me create the todo and start dispatching agents in parallel.\n\nI'll group the work into parallel batches of agents that don't conflict with each other.\n\nBatch 1 (parallel, no overlap):\n- Agent A: Fix `proactivity/engine.py` + `nexi/main.py` (both in nexi/)\n- Agent B: Fix `pg_episodic_store.py` (xnch/)\n- Agent C: Fix `vision_encoder.py` + `voice_daemon.py` (perception/)\n- Agent D: Fix `graph_store.py` + `graph_extractor.py` (memory/)\n\nBatch 2:\n- Agent E: Fix `xnch/main.py` APScheduler\n- Agent F: Fix `score_adapter.py` + `context_assembler.py`\n- Agent G: Fix `nexi_gateway.py` + `langfuse_client.py`\n\nBatch 3:\n- Agent H: Medium fixes (intent_interpreter, memory_guard, trust_model, cold_start_seeder, attention_filter)\n- Agent I: Low fixes (injection_guard, Dockerfile, K8s manifests)\n\nLet me create the todo first, then start dispatching.\n\nActually, since the task tool's agents have access to filesystem operations, I should choose the right agent type for each job:\n\n- `devtools/debugger` for bug fixes\n- `devtools/refactoring-specialist` for code improvements\n- `languages/python-pro` for Python-specific fixes\n- `devops/docker-specialist` for Docker fixes\n- `devops/kubernetes-specialist` for K8s fixes\n- `ai/llm-architect` for LLM-related fixes\n- `devops/incident-responder` might be good for critical fixes\n\nActually looking at the task tool system, each subagent has specific tool access and expertise. Let me plan the best agent-to-task mapping:\n\n- `languages/python-p"},"sessionId":"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI","timestamp":"2026-06-26T18:03:20.977Z"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mqv8oz7q_6e9f80075b22":{"observation":{"hookType":"task_completed","id":"obs_mqv8oz7q_6e9f80075b22","raw":{"completed":[],"in_progress":[{"content":"Critical: Fix proactivity/engine.py — get_failing_patterns, non-existent tables, port mismatch","priority":"high"},{"content":"Critical: Fix nexi/main.py — no-op URL replace at line 201","priority":"high"},{"content":"Critical: Fix pg_episodic_store.py — UUID-zero sentinel + retrieve_similar ignores query_text","priority":"high"},{"content":"Critical: Fix vision_encoder.py — wrong PIL import + wrong moondream method","priority":"high"},{"content":"Critical: Fix graph_store.py — sync dual-write + duplicate relations","priority":"high"},{"content":"High: Fix xnch/main.py — APScheduler lambda crashes on 3.13","priority":"high"},{"content":"High: Fix score_adapter.py — context_json vs context_snapshot","priority":"high"},{"content":"High: Fix context_assembler.py — bump_recall never called","priority":"high"},{"content":"High: Fix nexi_gateway.py — turn order + entity ID + private _redis access","priority":"high"},{"content":"High: Fix voice_daemon.py — int16→float32 + language detection","priority":"high"},{"content":"High