mplementedError in xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"InsecureKeyLengthWarning: HMAC key is 29 bytes (min 32 required)\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\",\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jvhh_cce47fe31c3a\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The full test suite was executed, revealing 4 failures and several warnings. Two failures are due to NotImplementedError in the episodic store and two are related to the intent interpreter, indicating regression or incomplete implementation in the persistence and interpretation layers.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"pytest execution in xnchSystems directory\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:26.497Z\",\"title\":\"Full test suite execution failure\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k09c_9aac7294080b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"NotImplementedError\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"API deprecation\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"test_execute failed with NotImplementedError\",\"test_fetchval failed with NotImplementedError\",\"The execute() and fetchval() methods in PgEpisodicStore are currently stubs that raise NotImplementedError\",\"The error message indicates a design decision to move away from direct SQL execution in favor of store_episode or agentmemory calls\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k09c_9aac7294080b\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Running pytest revealed that two tests in test_pg_episodic_store.py failed because the execute and fetchval methods in PgEpisodicStore have had their implementations removed in favor of higher-level APIs. This confirms the need to update the test suite or reimplement the required functionality.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running regression tests for PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:32.686Z\",\"title\":\"pytest failure in pg_episodic_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k1zx_cb338779dcf1\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"unit testing\",\"mocking async calls\",\"error handling fallback\",\"pytest\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"test_ambiguous_input_uses_llm failed: Expected _classify_with_llm to be awaited once, but it was awaited 0 times.\",\"test_llm_failure_falls_back failed: Expected ambiguity_score to be 0.5 on LLM failure, but got 0.0.\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k1zx_cb338779dcf1\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The pytest execution on the intent interpreter pipeline failed with two specific test regressions. One test failed to trigger the LLM classification path, and another failed to correctly assign a fallback ambiguity score when the LLM service fails.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running pytest on nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py reveals two assertion errors\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:34.939Z\",\"title\":\"pytest failures in intent_interpreter tests\",\"type\":\"error\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k6n4_c2e65b90505e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest async\",\"SQL integration testing\",\"mocking/patching\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests include test_execute for SQL UPDATE commands\",\"Tests include test_fetchval using patches for get_memories\",\"Tests include test_retrieve_similar_empty for handling empty results\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k6n4_c2e65b90505e\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"Read a segment of the episodic store test suite to understand the implementation of SQL execution and value fetching within the pg_episodic_store. This provides context for how the database interactions are validated.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting unit tests for PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:40.958Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k6xx_841aa3235cc8\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"asyncio testing\",\"mocking\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"unit testing\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"File: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"Tests use pytest and unittest.mock to validate PgEpisodicStore\",\"Includes an async fixture for managing store connection/disconnection\",\"Uses a mock for the 'create_memory' function\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k6xx_841aa3235cc8\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"The agent read the beginning of the test suite for the PostgreSQL episodic memory store. This file contains the core logic for testing episode creation and storage functionality within the xnch memory system.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining unit tests for PgEpisodicStore\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:41.347Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kapy_1a90c3f5981d\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"unit testing\",\"pg_episodic_store\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Command executed: pytest xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py with exclusions\",\"Two tests were deselected: test_execute and test_fetchval\",\"Test execution completed successfully in 0.45s\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kapy_1a90c3f5981d\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Ran a targeted pytest suite to ensure that tests other than the specific execution and fetchval tests pass in the pg_episodic_store module. This helps isolate regressions in the remaining test suite.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying remaining tests in test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:46.244Z\",\"title\":\"Run pytest on pg_episode_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kdu3_687fc5d0fe12\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"NotImplementedError\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests failed: 2 failed, 5 passed\",\"Errors caused by NotImplementedError in xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py:167\",\"Failed test cases: test_execute, test_fetchval\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kdu3_687fc5d0fe12\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"Running the pytest suite for the PostgreSQL episodic store revealed unimplemented methods in the implementation. This indicates that the core database interaction logic for execution and value fetching is missing.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Executing pytest on xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:50.282Z\",\"title\":\"Run pg_episodic_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"LiteLLM\",\"input injection guarding\",\"structured prompt engineering\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Uses LiteLLM for intent classification into QUERY, DECISION, EXECution, and ESCALATION.\",\"Implements a rule-based pre-filter stage before LLM processing.\",\"Includes security scanning via xnch.security.injection_guard.\",\"Defines a JSON schema for structured intent extraction including action_type, entity_class, and urgency.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the core intent classification module to understand how user inputs are parsed, validated for injections, and categorized into actionable intents. This is a critical component of the pipeline's decision-making logic.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Analyzing LiteLLM-backed intent classification logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.185Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"pytest fixture\",\"mocking async clients\",\"unit testing pipeline\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests cover IntentClass types: EXECUTION, QUERY, and ESCALATION.\",\"Uses pytest and unittest.mock to simulate LiteLLM responses.\",\"Includes tests for handling ambiguous inputs that trigger ClarificationRequired exceptions.\",\"Mocks httpx.AsyncClient to control LLM response simulation.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Read the test suite for the intent interpreter to understand how the system handles different intent classifications and ambiguity levels. This provides context for the expected behavior of the LLM-driven intent parsing logic.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining unit tests for the IntentInterpreter pipeline component\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.486Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_intent_interpreter.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"regex-based parsing\",\"hybrid retrieval\",\"entity extraction\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The system uses a two-stage approach: regex-based pre-filtering followed by memory-based recall.\",\"Regex rules map specific command prefixes (e.g., 'list', 'show', 'deploy') to IntentClasses (QUERY, EXECUTION, etc.).\",\"The `_rule_classify` function provides 1.0 confidence/0.0 ambiguity for regex matches.\",\"`_extract_entity` parses input to identify target entities like models, services, or databases.\",\"`_recall_intent` queries 'intent-classifications' memory to find previously matched intents.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the core intent parsing logic in the pipeline. The implementation uses a hybrid approach of deterministic regex rules and a vector/memory search for historical intents.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining the rule-based and memory-based intent classification logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:58.286Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"prompt injection detection\",\"regex-based security scanning\",\"security auditing\",\"risk scoring\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Uses regex patterns to detect common prompt injection strings (e.g., 'ignore previous instructions', 'DAN mode').\",\"Calculates a risk_score based on the proportion of matched patterns found.\",\"Integrates with EventLog to log security warnings when risk_score exceeds 0.1.\",\"Uses a dataclass InjectionResult to return scan results.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"The file contains the implementation for scanning text inputs for potential prompt injection attacks. It uses a predefined list of regex patterns to identify malicious instructions and logs attempts via an EventLog system.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspection of prompt injection detection logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:06.730Z\",\"title\":\"Read security/injection_guard.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"unit testing\",\"intent classification\",\"mocking async methods\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"IntentInterpreter correctly mapped 'xyzzyplex frobnicate' to EXECUTION/DEPLOY intent class via mock\",\"Mocked _classify_with_llm was not called during the test execution\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Executed a standalone Python script to verify if IntentInterpreter correctly processes input. The test showed the expected intent class and action type but revealed the LLM mock was not triggered as expected, suggesting a potential issue in the interpretation flow or method interception.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running unit test for IntentInterpreter with mocked LLM\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:18.594Z\",\"title\":\"Verify IntentInterpreter classification logic\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"rule-based engine\",\"unit testing\",\"mocking\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"_rule_classify returned None for input 'xyzzyplex frobnicate'\",\"_recall_intent successfully identified an EXECUTION intent with DEPLOY action\",\"LLM classification was bypassed via mock, confirming-rule-based logic paths\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Ran a standalone Python test script to debug the internal components of IntentInterpreter. The test verified that rule-based classification failed for the dummy string, but the recall mechanism successfully identified a high-urgency deployment intent.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying rule-based classification and intent recall\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:29.395Z\",\"title\":\"Debug intent interpreter logic via python script\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8lfsf_d4273e7e117e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"ChromaDB\",\