3ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"User query to retrieve architectural information for XNCH and NEXI\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:04:36.921Z\",\"title\":\"Recall Request: XNCH and NEXI Architecture\",\"type\":\"conversation\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8qn3t_1bd851c4194f\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"tool registry search\",\"memory smart search\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Found match for 'mcp__plugin_agentmemory_agentmemory__memory_smart_search'\",\"Total deferred tools in registry: 261\"],\"files\":[],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8qn3t_1bd851c4194f\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The system performed a targeted search within the tool registry to locate the specific memory smart search tool. This is part of navigating the available toolset for the agent.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Querying tool registry for specific memory search functionality\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:04:42.145Z\",\"title\":\"Search for memory smart search tool\",\"type\":\"search\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8qtse_5add5a12287a\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"system logging\",\"temporal tracking\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Current system timestamp recorded as 2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z\"],\"files\":[],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8qtse_5add5a12287a\",\"importance\":1,\"narrative\":\"A system notification was received containing a specific timestamp. This serves as a temporal marker for the ongoing session.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Log entry for 2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:04:50.846Z\",\"title\":\"System Timestamp Notification\",\"type\":\"notification\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8r7ae_35b323995dd4\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"graph extraction\",\"code review initialization\",\"duplicate edge prevention\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Retrieved several low-confidence lessons related to \\\"auto-import\\\" and code behavior.\",\"Found relevant task: \\\"Code Review Initialization: XNCH/Nexi Platform\\\".\",\"Retrieved notes about graph extraction issues (duplicate edges) and potential empty return values in existing logic.\"],\"files\":[],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8r7ae_35b323995dd4\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"Executed a semantic search in the memory agent to find architectural context for XNCH and Nexi. The search returned fragmented lessons regarding specific coding patterns and a recent task for a platform code review.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Querying historical lessons and observations regarding XNCH/Nexi platform\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:08.325Z\",\"title\":\"Memory search for XNCH and Nexi architecture\",\"type\":\"search\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8re10_5a3ec7e014ab\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"architecture planning\",\"pipeline discovery\",\"semantic search\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Search query targeted \\\"xnch nexi architecture plan phases pipeline\\\"\",\"Retrieved historical observations including task list updates, git diff summaries, and project file structure discovery\",\"Identified relevant historical sessions related to XNCH/Nexi Platform code review initialization\"],\"files\":[],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8re10_5a3ec7e014ab\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Performed a semantic search across the memory agent to retrieve context regarding the XNCH Nexi architecture plan. The search returned several related historical observations including project structure discovery and recent changes.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Querying historical observations for architecture phases and pipelines\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:17.079Z\",\"title\":\"Memory search for XNCH Nexi architecture plan\",\"type\":\"search\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8re79_2aa69a6b2830\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8re79_2aa69a6b2830\",\"raw\":{\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md\"},\"tool_name\":\"Read\",\"tool_output\":{\"file\":{\"content\":\"---\\nname: user-ck-san\\ndescription: \\\"User profile — ck-san, homelab AI builder targeting FDE/AI infrastructure roles\\\"\\nmetadata: \\n  node_type: memory\\n  type: user\\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\\n---\\n\\nck-san is building XNCH/Nexi as a portfolio-grade AI infrastructure system and for personal use. Background includes PCI DSS / Rakuten experience. Targeting FDE (Founding/Senior/Principal Engineer) and AI infrastructure roles.\\n\\n**Technical depth:** Comfortable with distributed systems, k8s, Python async, FastAPI, PostgreSQL. Has thought deeply about AI architecture (brain-to-stack mapping, memory decay, perception hierarchies). Not an ML researcher — systems engineer who orchestrates AI.\\n\\n**Preferred collaboration style:**\\n- Values architecture-first thinking over premature implementation\\n- Wants to use OSS components and wire them together rather than reinventing\\n- Prefers progressive enhancement: ship MVP fast, replace internals with owned IP over time\\n- Thinks in phases (sees the full roadmap, executes sequentially)\\n\\n**System details:**\\n- i7 node: control plane + memory (GTX 1650)\\n- i9 node: inference (RTX 3090, Gemma 4 26B)\\n- k8s already running on both nodes\\n- Uses Obsidian vault as knowledge base\\n- Plans: Telegram/WhatsApp as Nexi interface via OpenClaw\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md\",\"numLines\":26,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":26},\"type\":\"text\"}},\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:17.300Z\",\"toolInput\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md\"},\"toolName\":\"Read\",\"toolOutput\":{\"file\":{\"content\":\"---\\nname: user-ck-san\\ndescription: \\\"User profile — ck-san, homelab AI builder targeting FDE/AI infrastructure roles\\\"\\nmetadata: \\n  node_type: memory\\n  type: user\\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\\n---\\n\\nck-san is building XNCH/Nexi as a portfolio-grade AI infrastructure system and for personal use. Background includes PCI DSS / Rakuten experience. Targeting FDE (Founding/Senior/Principal Engineer) and AI infrastructure roles.\\n\\n**Technical depth:** Comfortable with distributed systems, k8s, Python async, FastAPI, PostgreSQL. Has thought deeply about AI architecture (brain-to-stack mapping, memory decay, perception hierarchies). Not an ML researcher — systems engineer who orchestrates AI.\\n\\n**Preferred collaboration style:**\\n- Values architecture-first thinking over premature implementation\\n- Wants to use OSS components and wire them together rather than reinventing\\n- Prefers progressive enhancement: ship MVP fast, replace internals with owned IP over time\\n- Thinks in phases (sees the full roadmap, executes sequentially)\\n\\n**System details:**\\n- i7 node: control plane + memory (GTX 1650)\\n- i9 node: inference (RTX 3090, Gemma 4 26B)\\n- k8s already running on both nodes\\n- Uses Obsidian vault as knowledge base\\n- Plans: Telegram/WhatsApp as Nexi interface via OpenClaw\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/user_ck_san.md\",\"numLines\":26,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":26},\"type\":\"text\"}},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8re79_1fc9ee3c1bdc\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8re79_1fc9ee3c1bdc\",\"raw\":{\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md\"},\"tool_name\":\"Read\",\"tool_output\":{\"file\":{\"content\":\"---\\nname: project-xnch-nexi\\ndescription: \\\"Core architecture context for the XNCH/Nexi homelab AI system — what it is, what exists, what's planned\\\"\\nmetadata: \\n  node_type: memory\\n  type: project\\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\\n---\\n\\nXNCH is a private AI orchestration platform (routing + memory + perception + observability). Nexi is the product face (OpenClaw interface wired to XNCH). They run on a 2-node homelab k8s cluster.\\n\\n**Why:** ck-san is building this as a portfolio piece and personal AI system. Long-term goal: FDE/AI infrastructure interviews. The architecture demonstrates systems thinking over ML research.\\n\\n**Hardware:**\\n- i7 + GTX 1650 4GB + 16GB RAM = Memory Node (xnch control plane, Redis, PostgreSQL+pgvector, Kuzu, LiteLLM, perception)\\n- i9 + RTX 3090 24GB + 48GB RAM = Inference Node (Gemma 4 26B via vLLM, nexi decision engine, Mem0, Zep, OpenClaw)\\n\\n**Current codebase state (~65% complete):**\\n- `xnch/` — governance/policy/memory/auth control plane. All 9 routes exist. Auth, episodic store (SQLite), policy engine, audit JSONL all working.\\n- `nexi/` — decision pipeline (intent → options → policy filter → score → verdict → dispatch). Evaluator and selector solid; intent_interpreter, option_generator, plan_compiler are stubs.\\n- `xnch/learning/` — pattern_extractor, score_adapter, policy_candidates all stubs.\\n- No Docker/k8s files, no LiteLLM, no pgvector, no Kuzu, no Langfuse, no perception.\\n\\n**Approved master plan:** `/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md`\\n\\n**Execution sequence:** Phase 0 (fix 4 critical gaps) → Phase 1 (XnchMemory pgvector+Kuzu) → Phase 2 (LiteLLM routing) → Phase 3 (intent interpreter real impl) → Phase 6 (OpenClaw → Nexi live) → Phase 5 (Langfuse) → Phase 4 (perception) → Phase 7 (learning loop) → Phase 8 (k8s manifests)\\n\\n**How to apply:** Always consult the plan file before implementing. Phase 0 must complete before any other phase. After Phase 6, Nexi is live — everything after is progressive enhancement.\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md\",\"numLines\":29,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":29},\"type\":\"text\"}},\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:17.300Z\",\"toolInput\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md\"},\"toolName\":\"Read\",\"toolOutput\":{\"file\":{\"content\":\"---\\nname: project-xnch-nexi\\ndescription: \\\"Core architecture context for the XNCH/Nexi homelab AI system — what it is, what exists, what's planned\\\"\\nmetadata: \\n  node_type: memory\\n  type: project\\n  originSessionId: 04c2a739-32bf-4093-a34d-5b889775279d\\n---\\n\\nXNCH is a private AI orchestration platform (routing + memory + perception + observability). Nexi is the product face (OpenClaw interface wired to XNCH). They run on a 2-node homelab k8s cluster.\\n\\n**Why:** ck-san is building this as a portfolio piece and personal AI system. Long-term goal: FDE/AI infrastructure interviews. The architecture demonstrates systems thinking over ML research.\\n\\n**Hardware:**\\n- i7 + GTX 1650 4GB + 16GB RAM = Memory Node (xnch control plane, Redis, PostgreSQL+pgvector, Kuzu, LiteLLM, perception)\\n- i9 + RTX 3090 24GB + 48GB RAM = Inference Node (Gemma 4 26B via vLLM, nexi decision engine, Mem0, Zep, OpenClaw)\\n\\n**Current codebase state (~65% complete):**\\n- `xnch/` — governance/policy/memory/auth control plane. All 9 routes exist. Auth, episodic store (SQLite), policy engine, audit JSONL all working.\\n- `nexi/` — decision pipeline (intent → options → policy filter → score → verdict → dispatch). Evaluator and selector solid; intent_interpreter, option_generator, plan_compiler are stubs.\\n- `xnch/learning/` — pattern_extractor, score_adapter, policy_candidates all stubs.\\n- No Docker/k8s files, no LiteLLM, no pgvector, no Kuzu, no Langfuse, no perception.\\n\\n**Approved master plan:** `/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md`\\n\\n**Execution sequence:** Phase 0 (fix 4 critical gaps) → Phase 1 (XnchMemory pgvector+Kuzu) → Phase 2 (LiteLLM routing) → Phase 3 (intent interpreter real impl) → Phase 6 (OpenClaw → Nexi live) → Phase 5 (Langfuse) → Phase 4 (perception) → Phase 7 (learning loop) → Phase 8 (k8s manifests)\\n\\n**How to apply:** Always consult the plan file before implementing. Phase 0 must complete before any other phase. After Phase 6, Nexi is live — everything after is progressive enhancement.\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/Users/xnch/.claude/projects/-Users-xnch-xnchSystems/memory/project_xnch_nexi.md\",\"numLines\":29,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":29},\"type\":\"text\"}},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8rjbp_6ea4caad981e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Multi-layer memory architecture\",\"Hierarchical storage (Redis, PostgreSQL, Kuzu)\",\"Inference routing proxy\",\"Distributed hardware assignment\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Current system implements ~65% of governance/decision core\",\"Critical naming collision: XNCH (platform) vs Nexi (product interface)\",\"Identified 4 critical gaps (C-1 to C-4) regarding scoring dimensions, DAG schema, DSL enums, and pattern extractor grouping\",\"Architecture requires migration from SQLite to PostgreSQL/pgvector for Layer 2 memory\",\"Hardware split: i7 node for memory/control plane, i9 node for inference (vLLM/Gemma 4)\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/.claude/plans/fluffy-percolating-cosmos.md\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8rjbp_6ea4caad981e\",\"importance\":7,\"narrative\":\"Read the master architecture plan to understand the roadmap for completing the XNCH/Nexi system, including the transition from SQLite to a more robust memory hierarchy and the distinction between the XNCH platform and the Nexi product layer.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Reviewing XNCH/Nexi end-to-end architecture plan\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:23.946Z\",\"title\":\"Read architecture plan\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8rvl0_7c43f614a95f\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[],\"confidence\":0.75,\"facts\":[\"The subagent has finished its assigned task\"],\"files\":[],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8rvl0_7c43f614a95f\",\"importance\":1,\"narrative\":\"The subagent was stopped, indicating that the specific task or sub-process it was managing has reached a terminal state. This signifies a transition back to the primary agent's control.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Termination of subagent process\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:05:39.833Z\",\"title\":\"Subagent execution completed\",\"type\":\"other\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8u0ag_100447887520\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"git history\",\"branch management\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"HEAD is at commit 29079db (v0)\",\"Recent branches include v4-localOC and v3\",\"Commit 43ad614 (v2) contained docs update\",\"Initial commit is 984b095 (main)\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8u0ag_100447887520\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"The user executed a git log command to inspect the commit history of the nexi directory. This reveals the current branch state and recent development activity within that subdirectory.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Checking recent commit history in nexi/ folder\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:19.244Z\",\"title\":\"Git log for nexi directory\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8u0se_420c491ae22b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"fallback chain\",\"rule-based templates\",\"intent-based action specs\",\"model adapter pattern\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The nexi/ directory was recently initialized with new files.\",\"ModelAdapter implements a 4-stage fallback chain: vllm-primary, vllms-secondary, llama-cpp-python, and rule-based templates.\",\"Rule-based templates define specific action types (READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, etc.) for different IntentClasses (QUERY, DECISION, EXECUTION).\",\"New package structure includes nexi/__init__.py, nexi/adapters/__init__.py, and nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py.\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/nexi/__init__.py\",\"nexi/nexi/adapters/__init__.py\",\"nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8u0se_420c491ae22b\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"The git diff shows the initial creation of the Nexi decision engine. It introduces a multi-layered model adapter with a fallback mechanism and a rule-based template system for handling different intent classes.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Reviewing recent changes to the nexi/ directory\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:19.885Z\",\"title\":\"New commit: Initialization of Nexi project\",\"type\":\"discovery\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8u68j_698a31d7c038\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LiteLLM proxy integration\",\"Dynamic request routing\",\"Model fallback patterns\",\"Inference abstraction\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"ModelAdapter is transitioning from a hardcoded vllm-primary/secondary fallback chain to a LiteLLM proxy-based approach.\",\"Introduced `classify_request` from `xnch.routing.classifier` to determine model routing.\",\"Refactored `_call_vllm` to `_call_litellm` which accepts a specific `model_name` derived from request classification.\",\"Updated fallback chain to use `litellm_proxy_url` and `litellm_proxy_timeout_s` from settings.\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\",\"nexi/nexi/config.py\",\"nexi/nexi/main.py\",\"nexi/nexi/models/__init__.py\",\"nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\",\"nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\",\"nexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py\",\"nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\",\"nexi/nexi/utils/audit.py\",\"nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8u68j_698a31d7c038\",\"importance\":7,\"narrative\":\"The git diff shows a significant architectural shift in how the ModelAdapter handles inference requests, moving from a static multi-stage fallback chain to a dynamic routing system using LiteLLM and a request classifier. This change introduces more flexibility by allowing request-specific model selection via a routing agent.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Reviewing modifications to model adapter and routing logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:26.950Z\",\"title\":\"Git diff of unstaged changes in nexi codebase\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8ua51_59d7b5905165\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LiteLLM proxy\",\"request routing\",\"LLM observability\",\"dynamic model selection\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Modified nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py to replace direct vLLM calls with a LiteLLM proxy approach.\",\"Introduced `classify_request` from `xnch.routing.classifier` to determine model route based on input.\",\"Added `trace_llm_call` from `xnch.observability.langfuse_client` for observability.\",\"Deprecated the explicit multi-step vLLM fallback chain in favor of a unified LiteLLM endpoint usage.\",\"The `_call_litellm` method now accepts a dynamic `model_name` determined by the classifier.\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ua51_59d7b5905165\",\"importance\":7,\"narrative\":\"The ModelAdapter has been refactored to use a LiteLLM proxy instead of a manually managed vLLM fallback chain. This change introduces request classification to dynamically route prompts to appropriate models and adds observability via Langfuse.\",\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"subtitle\":\"Migrating from hardcoded vLLM chain to LiteLLM proxy with dynamic routing\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:32.008Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor ModelAdapter to use LiteLLM and Request Classification\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8ubxt_295a0e30ad51\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ubxt_295a0e30ad51\",\"raw\":{\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD --name-only -- nexi/\",\"description\":\"List changed nexi files only\"},\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_output\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\\nnexi/nexi/config.py\\nnexi/nexi/main.py\\nnexi/nexi/models/__init__.py\\nnexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\nnexi/nexi/utils/audit.py\\nnexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"}},\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:34.340Z\",\"toolInput\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD --name-only -- nexi/\",\"description\":\"List changed nexi files only\"},\"toolName\":\"Bash\",\"toolOutput\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"nexi/nexi/adapters/model_adapter.py\\nnexi/nexi/config.py\\nnexi/nexi/main.py\\nnexi/nexi/models/__init__.py\\nnexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/option_generator.py\\nnexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\nnexi/nexi/utils/audit.py\\nnexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"}},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8ue7o_0efbad16c9a7\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ue7o_0efbad16c9a7\",\"raw\":{\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py 2>/dev/null | head -100\",\"description\":\"Diff of plan_compiler.py changes\"},\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_output\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"diff --git c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\nindex 701349e..987c4e7 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 10a — Action spec validation before verdict submission.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n-from typing import Any\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 10a — Action spec validation before verdict submission.\\n \\n+Converts a PlanOption into a single-node CompiledDAG for execution dispatch.\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+from ..models.dag import DAGNode, CompiledDAG\\n from ..models.options import ActionSpec, PlanOption\\n \\n \\n@@ -16,8 +18,8 @@ class PlanCompilationError(Exception):\\n     pass\\n \\n \\n-def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n-    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validates the selected option's action_spec. Raises PlanCompilationError on failure.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> CompiledDAG:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validates the selected option and returns a single-node CompiledDAG.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     spec = opt.action_spec\\n \\n     if not spec.type:\\n@@ -28,11 +30,17 @@ def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n         raise PlanCompilationError(\\\"action_spec.params must not be null\\\")\\n \\n     if spec.type.upper() not in _KNOWN_ACTION_TYPES:\\n-        # Unknown types are preserved (per Contract 4) but logged\\n         pass\\n \\n-    return {\\n-        \\\"type\\\": spec.type.upper(),\\n-        \\\"target\\\": spec.target,\\n-        \\\"params\\\": spec.params,\\n-    }\\n+    node = DAGNode(\\n+        node_id=str(opt.option_id),\\n+        action_type=spec.type.upper(),\\n+        target=spec.target,\\n+        params=spec.params,\\n+        depends_on=[],\\n+    )\\n+    return CompiledDAG(\\n+        nodes=[node],\\n+        edges=[],\\n+        entry_node=node.node_id,\\n+    )\"}},\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:37.284Z\",\"toolInput\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py 2>/dev/null | head -100\",\"description\":\"Diff of plan_compiler.py changes\"},\"toolName\":\"Bash\",\"toolOutput\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"diff --git c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\nindex 701349e..987c4e7 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/plan_compiler.py\\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 10a — Action spec validation before verdict submission.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n-from typing import Any\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 10a — Action spec validation before verdict submission.\\n \\n+Converts a PlanOption into a single-node CompiledDAG for execution dispatch.\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+from ..models.dag import DAGNode, CompiledDAG\\n from ..models.options import ActionSpec, PlanOption\\n \\n \\n@@ -16,8 +18,8 @@ class PlanCompilationError(Exception):\\n     pass\\n \\n \\n-def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n-    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validates the selected option's action_spec. Raises PlanCompilationError on failure.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> CompiledDAG:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validates the selected option and returns a single-node CompiledDAG.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n     spec = opt.action_spec\\n \\n     if not spec.type:\\n@@ -28,11 +30,17 @@ def compile_action_spec(opt: PlanOption) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n         raise PlanCompilationError(\\\"action_spec.params must not be null\\\")\\n \\n     if spec.type.upper() not in _KNOWN_ACTION_TYPES:\\n-        # Unknown types are preserved (per Contract 4) but logged\\n         pass\\n \\n-    return {\\n-        \\\"type\\\": spec.type.upper(),\\n-        \\\"target\\\": spec.target,\\n-        \\\"params\\\": spec.params,\\n-    }\\n+    node = DAGNode(\\n+        node_id=str(opt.option_id),\\n+        action_type=spec.type.upper(),\\n+        target=spec.target,\\n+        params=spec.params,\\n+        depends_on=[],\\n+    )\\n+    return CompiledDAG(\\n+        nodes=[node],\\n+        edges=[],\\n+        entry_node=node.node_id,\\n+    )\"}},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8uepy_fb7bc3c12ae3\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8uepy_fb7bc3c12ae3\",\"raw\":{\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/models/intent.py 2>/dev/null | head -80 && echo \\\"===\\\" && git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py 2>/dev/null | head -80\",\"description\":\"Diff of intent model and interpreter changes\"},\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_output\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"diff --git c/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py w/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\nindex 5362dc2..78de710 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\n@@ -49,3 +49,5 @@ class Intent(BaseModel):\\n     urgency: Urgency = Urgency.NORMAL\\n     ambiguity_score: Annotated[float, Field(ge=0.0, le=1.0)]\\n     raw_input_hash: str\\n+    raw_input: str = \\\"\\\"\\n+    clarifications_needed: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n===\\ndiff --git c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\nindex 0fa9f4a..d7dbb7a 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\n@@ -1,18 +1,60 @@\\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4). LiteLLM-backed classifier.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n import hashlib\\n+import json\\n import re\\n from typing import Any\\n from uuid import UUID\\n \\n+import httpx\\n+from agentmemory import create_memory, search_memory\\n+\\n+from ..config import settings\\n from ..models.intent import Intent, IntentClass, ActionType, Urgency\\n from ..utils.audit import emit_event\\n+from xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input, InjectionResult\\n+\\n+\\n+class PolicyViolation(Exception):\\n+    pass\\n+\\n+\\n+_CLASSIFICATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are an intent classifier for a systems-management agent.\\n+Classify the user's raw input into one of these intent classes:\\n+\\n+- QUERY: Read-only information retrieval (list, show, get, fetch, display)\\n+- DECISION: Planning, design, recommendation, analysis for decision support\\n+- EXECUTION: Mutating actions (deploy, rollback, write, delete, backup, run)\\n+- ESCALATION: Escalate to human operator\\n+\\n+Respond with a JSON object using this schema:\\n+{\\n+  \\\"intent_class\\\": \\\"QUERY|DECISION|EXECUTION|ESCALATION\\\",\\n+  \\\"action_type\\\": \\\"<appropriate action from the list below>\\\",\\n+  \\\"entity_class\\\": \\\"<guessed entity type: ML_MODEL|SERVICE|DATABASE|CLUSTER|FILE|SCRIPT|SCHEMA|RESOURCE>\\\",\\n+  \\\"urgency\\\": \\\"LOW|NORMAL|HIGH|CRITICAL\\\",\\n+  \\\"entity_id\\\": \\\"<the noun phrase identifying the target>\\\",\\n+  \\\"clarifications_needed\\\": [\\\"<question if ambiguous>\\\"]\\n+}\\n+\\n+Action types by class:\\n+QUERY → READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, QUERY\\n+DECISION → PLAN, ANALYZE\\n+EXECUTION → DEPLOY, ROLLBACK, BACKUP, RESTORE, WRITE_FILE, DELETE_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, RUN_SCRIPT, STAGE, MUTATE\\n+ESCALATION → ESCALATE\\n+\\n+If the input is ambiguous (multiple interpretations possible), populates clarifications_needed\\n+with specific questions to disambiguate. Otherwise leave it empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n \\n \\n class ClarificationRequired(Exception):\\n-    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float) -> None:\\n+    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float, questions: list[str] | None = None) -> None:\\n         self.session_id = session_id\\n         self.ambiguity_score = ambiguity_score\\n-        super().__init__(f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\")\\n+        self.questions = questions or []\\n+        msg = f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\"\\n+        if self.questions:\\n+            msg += f\\\"; questions: {'; '.join(self.questions)}\\\"\\n+        super().__init__(msg)\\n \\n \\n # Stage 1: rule-based pre-filter (confidence=1.0, ambiguity=0.0)\\n@@ -39,10 +81,8 @@ def _rule_classify(raw_input: str) -> tuple[IntentClass, str, float, float] | No\\n \\n \\n def _extract_entity(raw_input: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\\n-    # Minimal entity extraction for v0 — returns the noun phrase after the verb\\n     tokens = raw_input.strip().split()\\n-    entity_id = tokens[1] if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n-    # Crude class heuristic\\n+    entity_id = \\\" \\\".join(tokens[1:]) if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n     entity_class_hints = {\\n         \\\"model\\\": \\\"ML_MODEL\\\", \\\"service\\\": \\\"SERVICE\\\", \\\"db\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\",\\n         \\\"database\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\", \\\"cluster\\\": \\\"CLUSTER\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"FILE\\\",\"}},\"sessionId\":\"8a12ce37-9817-49dc-8990-dd863ab7acf0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:37.944Z\",\"toolInput\":{\"command\":\"git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/models/intent.py 2>/dev/null | head -80 && echo \\\"===\\\" && git diff HEAD -- nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py 2>/dev/null | head -80\",\"description\":\"Diff of intent model and interpreter changes\"},\"toolName\":\"Bash\",\"toolOutput\":{\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"stderr\":\"\",\"stdout\":\"diff --git c/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py w/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\nindex 5362dc2..78de710 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/models/intent.py\\n@@ -49,3 +49,5 @@ class Intent(BaseModel):\\n     urgency: Urgency = Urgency.NORMAL\\n     ambiguity_score: Annotated[float, Field(ge=0.0, le=1.0)]\\n     raw_input_hash: str\\n+    raw_input: str = \\\"\\\"\\n+    clarifications_needed: list[str] = Field(default_factory=list)\\n===\\ndiff --git c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\nindex 0fa9f4a..d7dbb7a 100644\\n--- c/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\n+++ w/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\n@@ -1,18 +1,60 @@\\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Step 3 — Intent Normalization (Contract 4). LiteLLM-backed classifier.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n import hashlib\\n+import json\\n import re\\n from typing import Any\\n from uuid import UUID\\n \\n+import httpx\\n+from agentmemory import create_memory, search_memory\\n+\\n+from ..config import settings\\n from ..models.intent import Intent, IntentClass, ActionType, Urgency\\n from ..utils.audit import emit_event\\n+from xnch.security.injection_guard import scan_input, InjectionResult\\n+\\n+\\n+class PolicyViolation(Exception):\\n+    pass\\n+\\n+\\n+_CLASSIFICATION_SYSTEM_PROMPT = \\\"\\\"\\\"You are an intent classifier for a systems-management agent.\\n+Classify the user's raw input into one of these intent classes:\\n+\\n+- QUERY: Read-only information retrieval (list, show, get, fetch, display)\\n+- DECISION: Planning, design, recommendation, analysis for decision support\\n+- EXECUTION: Mutating actions (deploy, rollback, write, delete, backup, run)\\n+- ESCALATION: Escalate to human operator\\n+\\n+Respond with a JSON object using this schema:\\n+{\\n+  \\\"intent_class\\\": \\\"QUERY|DECISION|EXECUTION|ESCALATION\\\",\\n+  \\\"action_type\\\": \\\"<appropriate action from the list below>\\\",\\n+  \\\"entity_class\\\": \\\"<guessed entity type: ML_MODEL|SERVICE|DATABASE|CLUSTER|FILE|SCRIPT|SCHEMA|RESOURCE>\\\",\\n+  \\\"urgency\\\": \\\"LOW|NORMAL|HIGH|CRITICAL\\\",\\n+  \\\"entity_id\\\": \\\"<the noun phrase identifying the target>\\\",\\n+  \\\"clarifications_needed\\\": [\\\"<question if ambiguous>\\\"]\\n+}\\n+\\n+Action types by class:\\n+QUERY → READ_FILE, LIST, ANALYZE, QUERY\\n+DECISION → PLAN, ANALYZE\\n+EXECUTION → DEPLOY, ROLLBACK, BACKUP, RESTORE, WRITE_FILE, DELETE_FILE, RUN_COMMAND, RUN_SCRIPT, STAGE, MUTATE\\n+ESCALATION → ESCALATE\\n+\\n+If the input is ambiguous (multiple interpretations possible), populates clarifications_needed\\n+with specific questions to disambiguate. Otherwise leave it empty.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n \\n \\n class ClarificationRequired(Exception):\\n-    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float) -> None:\\n+    def __init__(self, session_id: UUID, ambiguity_score: float, questions: list[str] | None = None) -> None:\\n         self.session_id = session_id\\n         self.ambiguity_score = ambiguity_score\\n-        super().__init__(f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\")\\n+        self.questions = questions or []\\n+        msg = f\\\"Ambiguity score {ambiguity_score:.2f} exceeds threshold\\\"\\n+        if self.questions:\\n+            msg += f\\\"; questions: {'; '.join(self.questions)}\\\"\\n+        super().__init__(msg)\\n \\n \\n # Stage 1: rule-based pre-filter (confidence=1.0, ambiguity=0.0)\\n@@ -39,10 +81,8 @@ def _rule_classify(raw_input: str) -> tuple[IntentClass, str, float, float] | No\\n \\n \\n def _extract_entity(raw_input: str) -> tuple[str, str]:\\n-    # Minimal entity extraction for v0 — returns the noun phrase after the verb\\n     tokens = raw_input.strip().split()\\n-    entity_id = tokens[1] if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n-    # Crude class heuristic\\n+    entity_id = \\\" \\\".join(tokens[1:]) if len(tokens) > 1 else \\\"unknown\\\"\\n     entity_class_hints = {\\n         \\\"model\\\": \\\"ML_MODEL\\\", \\\"service\\\": \\\"SERVICE\\\", \\\"db\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\",\\n         \\\"database\\\": \\\"DATABASE\\\", \\\"cluster\\\": \\\"CLUSTER\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"FILE\\\",\"}},\"type\":\"raw\"}}\u0000\u0000\u0000�\u0013\u0002\u0000\b{��\n\\ No newline at end of file\n","status":"added"},{"additions":1,"deletions":0,"file":"data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF.bin","patch":"Index: data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF.bin\n===================================================================\n--- data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF.bin\t\n+++ data/stream_store/stream%3Amem-live%3Ases_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF.bin\t\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\n+{\"obs_mqv8uffn_87f7be0572bc\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"session_updated\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8uffn_87f7be0572bc\",\"raw\":{\"additions\":null,\"deletions\":null,\"files\":null,\"parentID\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"title\":\"Fix cold_start + attention + memory_guard (@languages/python-pro subagent)\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:38.913Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8uffp_ebbd6d4f5497\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"prompt_submit\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8uffp_ebbd6d4f5497\",\"raw\":{\"agent\":\"languages/python-pro\",\"files\":[],\"model\":{\"modelID\":\"big-pickle\",\"providerID\":\"opencode\"},\"parts_summary\":[\"text\"],\"prompt\":\"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\\n\\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py — full scan with hours=999999 (Medium)**\\n- Line 48: `list_recent(hours=999999)` loads all 5000 agentmemory episodes on every cold-start check. Fix: Use `search_memory` to check for identity type entries efficiently:\\n```python\\nexisting = search_memory(\\\"episodes\\\", \\\"identity\\\", n_results=1, filter_metadata={\\\"type\\\": \\\"identity\\\"})\\nif existing:\\n    logger.info(\\\"Identity already seeded (%d entries found), skipping\\\", len(existing))\\n    return\\n```\\nYou need to add `from agentmemory import search_memory` to imports. But first check if `search_memory` is already used in the file.\\n\\nActually, look at the current code first. The function is `cold_start_seeder.seed_if_needed()`. The fix should:\\n1. Replace the `list_recent(999999)` call with a targeted `search_memory` call\\n2. If results exist, log and return early\\n3. The rest of the function stays the same\\n\\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py — create_task from sync context (Medium)**\\n- Lines 65-70: `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` is called from `evaluate()`, a synchronous method called from a watchdog thread. `asyncio.create_task()` requires a running event loop. Fix:\\n  - Replace `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` with:\\n```python\\ntask = asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())\\ntask.add_done_callback(lambda t: t.exception() and logger.error(\\\"consolidation failed: %s\\\", t.exception()))\\n```\\n  - At minimum, keep the existing try/except but store the task reference and add error callback.\\n\\nRead the current code to see exactly what's there.\\n\\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py — validate_memory_write never called (Medium)**\\nThis isn't a code fix — it's a wiring issue. Check:\\n1. Read `memory_guard.py` to see the `validate_memory_write` API\\n2. Read `nexi_gateway.py` to find `store_episode()` calls\\n3. If those calls don't have validation, add it.\\n\\nThe fix should add `validate_memory_write` calls before each `store_episode()` call in nexi_gateway.py:\\n```python\\nfrom xnch.security.memory_guard import validate_memory_write\\n# Before store_episode():\\nvalidation = validate_memory_write(content, actor_role, trust_level)\\n# If validation fails, return 403 or log warning\\n```\\n\\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).\",\"variant\":null},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:38.915Z\",\"userPrompt\":\"Fix 3 bugs. Read the files first, then apply edits.\\n\\n**Bug 1: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py — full scan with hours=999999 (Medium)**\\n- Line 48: `list_recent(hours=999999)` loads all 5000 agentmemory episodes on every cold-start check. Fix: Use `search_memory` to check for identity type entries efficiently:\\n```python\\nexisting = search_memory(\\\"episodes\\\", \\\"identity\\\", n_results=1, filter_metadata={\\\"type\\\": \\\"identity\\\"})\\nif existing:\\n    logger.info(\\\"Identity already seeded (%d entries found), skipping\\\", len(existing))\\n    return\\n```\\nYou need to add `from agentmemory import search_memory` to imports. But first check if `search_memory` is already used in the file.\\n\\nActually, look at the current code first. The function is `cold_start_seeder.seed_if_needed()`. The fix should:\\n1. Replace the `list_recent(999999)` call with a targeted `search_memory` call\\n2. If results exist, log and return early\\n3. The rest of the function stays the same\\n\\n**Bug 2: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py — create_task from sync context (Medium)**\\n- Lines 65-70: `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` is called from `evaluate()`, a synchronous method called from a watchdog thread. `asyncio.create_task()` requires a running event loop. Fix:\\n  - Replace `asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())` with:\\n```python\\ntask = asyncio.create_task(run_consolidation())\\ntask.add_done_callback(lambda t: t.exception() and logger.error(\\\"consolidation failed: %s\\\", t.exception()))\\n```\\n  - At minimum, keep the existing try/except but store the task reference and add error callback.\\n\\nRead the current code to see exactly what's there.\\n\\n**Bug 3: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/memory_guard.py — validate_memory_write never called (Medium)**\\nThis isn't a code fix — it's a wiring issue. Check:\\n1. Read `memory_guard.py` to see the `validate_memory_write` API\\n2. Read `nexi_gateway.py` to find `store_episode()` calls\\n3. If those calls don't have validation, add it.\\n\\nThe fix should add `validate_memory_write` calls before each `store_episode()` call in nexi_gateway.py:\\n```python\\nfrom xnch.security.memory_guard import validate_memory_write\\n# Before store_episode():\\nvalidation = validate_memory_write(content, actor_role, trust_level)\\n# If validation fails, return 403 or log warning\\n```\\n\\nReturn a summary of every change (file, line, what changed).\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8ufg1_3d544dd70105\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"session_status\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ufg1_3d544dd70105\",\"raw\":{\"attempt\":null,\"message\":\"\",\"status_type\":\"busy\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae25260fferIk2T6UHXhI3mF\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:07:38.9