http://localhost:8002\\\"` to nexi/nexi/config.py, then use `settings.execution_runner_url` in main.py. Read nexi/nexi/config.py first to see the Settings class.\\n\\nVerify: Run `cd /Users/xnch/xnchSystems && .venv/bin/python -c \\\"from nexi.nexi.config import settings; print(settings.execution_runner_url)\\\"` after adding the config key.\\n\\nReturn a summary of every change you make (file, line, what changed).\",\"variant\":null},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.114Z\",\"userPrompt\":\"Fix 3 critical bugs in the nexi package. Read the files first, then apply edits.\\n\\n**Bug 1: nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py**\\n- Line 56: `pattern_store.get_failing_patterns()` doesn't exist. The correct method is `await pattern_store.fetch_low_success(max_success_rate=0.4, min_confidence=0.5)`. The `check_and_queue` method must become async.\\n- Lines 75-77, 113-115: Queries `consolidation_jobs` and `extractor_runs` tables that don't exist. Replace with queries against `system_state` table:\\n  - Rule 2: `SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_consolidation_run'`\\n  - Rule 4: `SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_extraction_run'`\\n- Line 93: Health check URL is `http://i9-node:8080/health` but the service exposes port 8000. Read from config: `settings.vllm_health_url` with default `http://vllm-gemma4:8000/health`. Also wire `_http` in the factory (check how it's initialized).\\n\\n**Bug 2: nexi/nexi/main.py**\\n- Line 201: `settings.xnch_base_url.replace(\\\"8001\\\", \\\"8001\\\")` is a no-op (replaces 8001 with 8001). Change to use a config key or stopgap: add `execution_runner_url: str = \\\"http://localhost:8002\\\"` to nexi/nexi/config.py, then use `settings.execution_runner_url` in main.py. Read nexi/nexi/config.py first to see the Settings class.\\n\\nVerify: Run `cd /Users/xnch/xnchSystems && .venv/bin/python -c \\\"from nexi.nexi.config import settings; print(settings.execution_runner_url)\\\"` after adding the config key.\\n\\nReturn a summary of every change you make (file, line, what changed).\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p5s8_903d504da189\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"config_loaded\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p5s8_903d504da189\",\"raw\":{\"agents\":[\"languages/python-pro\",\"ai/data-engineer\",\"ai/data-scientist\",\"ai/ai-engineer\",\"ai/search-specialist\",\"ai/mlops-engineer\",\"ai/llm-architect\",\"ai/ml-engineer\",\"ai/data-analyst\",\"ai/prompt-engineer\",\"docs/documentation-engineer\",\"docs/api-documenter\",\"docs/diagram-architect\",\"docs/technical-writer\",\"devtools/refactoring-specialist\",\"devtools/microservices-architect\",\"devtools/debugger\",\"devtools/performance-engineer\",\"devtools/legacy-modernizer\",\"devtools/qa-expert\",\"devtools/test-automator\",\"devtools/code-reviewer\",\"devops/aws-specialist\",\"devops/linux-admin\",\"devops/kubernetes-specialist\",\"devops/incident-responder\",\"devops/docker-specialist\",\"devops/sre-engineer\",\"devops/platform-engineer\",\"devops/ci-cd-engineer\",\"devops/terraform-specialist\",\"data-api/postgres-pro\",\"data-api/graphql-architect\",\"data-api/api-architect\",\"data-api/sql-pro\",\"data-api/database-architect\",\"data-api/redis-specialist\"],\"autoupdate\":null,\"mcp_servers\":[\"vercel\",\"spotify\",\"document-reader\",\"agentmemory\"],\"model\":null,\"permission\":null,\"providers\":[],\"theme\":null},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.124Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p5sh_9619d68263db\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"session_status\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p5sh_9619d68263db\",\"raw\":{\"attempt\":null,\"message\":\"\",\"status_type\":\"busy\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.137Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p5si_ab025292fd1b\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"assistant_message\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p5si_ab025292fd1b\",\"raw\":{\"cost\":0,\"duration_ms\":null,\"error\":null,\"finish\":null,\"messageID\":\"msg_f0519ed910027EzWj9gBdP359N\",\"mode\":\"languages/python-pro\",\"modelID\":\"big-pickle\",\"parentID\":\"msg_f0519ed750022aV8dXRicZ0Rra\",\"providerID\":\"opencode\",\"tokens\":{\"cache_read\":0,\"cache_write\":0,\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"reasoning\":0}},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.137Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p5vs_41df181c7f91\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"session_diff\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p5vs_41df181c7f91\",\"raw\":{\"additions\":0,\"deletions\":0,\"diffs\":[],\"files\":[]},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.255Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p5w0_b16e57339dbe\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"llm_params\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p5w0_b16e57339dbe\",\"raw\":{\"agent\":\"languages/python-pro\",\"context_limit\":200000,\"cost_1k_input\":0,\"cost_1k_output\":0,\"max_output_tokens\":32000,\"model\":\"opencode/big-pickle\",\"provider_url\":\"https://opencode.ai/zen/v1\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:33.264Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p8d3_482993542eb4\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"reasoning\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p8d3_482993542eb4\",\"raw\":{\"messageID\":\"msg_f0519ed910027EzWj9gBdP359N\",\"text\":\"\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:36.469Z\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p8to_c31c435f1bfe\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p8to_c31c435f1bfe\",\"raw\":{\"attachments\":[],\"call_id\":\"call_00_Hm0vZKGGcZMqFcoBxVmy2122\",\"duration_ms\":5,\"metadata\":{\"loaded\":[],\"preview\":\"from __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport logging\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\\nfrom uuid import uuid4\\n\\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass ProactivityEvent:\\n    trigger: str\\n    message: str\\n    priority: int = 0\\n    expires_at: datetime = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=2))\\n\\n    @property\\n    def expired(self) -> bool:\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py\",\"tool_input\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py\\\"}\",\"tool_name\":\"read\",\"tool_output\":\"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: from __future__ import annotations\\n2: \\n3: import json\\n4: import logging\\n5: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\\n6: from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\\n7: from uuid import uuid4\\n8: \\n9: logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n10: \\n11: \\n12: @dataclass\\n13: class ProactivityEvent:\\n14:     trigger: str\\n15:     message: str\\n16:     priority: int = 0\\n17:     expires_at: datetime = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=2))\\n18: \\n19:     @property\\n20:     def expired(self) -> bool:\\n21:         return datetime.now(timezone.utc) > self.expires_at\\n22: \\n23:     def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n24:         return {\\n25:             \\\"trigger\\\": self.trigger,\\n26:             \\\"message\\\": self.message,\\n27:             \\\"priority\\\": self.priority,\\n28:             \\\"expires_at\\\": self.expires_at.isoformat(),\\n29:         }\\n30: \\n31:     @classmethod\\n32:     def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> ProactivityEvent:\\n33:         return cls(\\n34:             trigger=d[\\\"trigger\\\"],\\n35:             message=d[\\\"message\\\"],\\n36:             priority=d.get(\\\"priority\\\", 0),\\n37:             expires_at=datetime.fromisoformat(d[\\\"expires_at\\\"]),\\n38:         )\\n39: \\n40: \\n41: class ProactivityEngine:\\n42:     def __init__(self, redis_client, http_client=None):\\n43:         self._redis = redis_client\\n44:         self._http = http_client\\n45: \\n46:     async def check_and_queue(\\n47:         self,\\n48:         pattern_store=None,\\n49:         db_path=None,\\n50:     ) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\\n51:         events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\\n52:         now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\\n53: \\n54:         if pattern_store is not None:\\n55:             try:\\n56:                 patterns = await pattern_store.fetch_low_success(max_success_rate=0.4, min_confidence=0.5)\\n57:                 for p in patterns:\\n58:                     events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n59:                         trigger=\\\"stale_pattern\\\",\\n60:                         message=(\\n61:                             f\\\"ck-san, the {p.get('action_type', 'unknown')} pattern for \\\"\\n62:                             f\\\"{p.get('intent_class', 'unknown')} is failing 60%+ of the time. \\\"\\n63:                             f\\\"Want me to draft a policy candidate fix?\\\"\\n64:                         ),\\n65:                         priority=3,\\n66:                         expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\\n67:                     ))\\n68:             except Exception as e:\\n69:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 1 (stale pattern) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n70: \\n71:         if db_path is not None:\\n72:             try:\\n73:                 import aiosqlite\\n74:                 async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\\n75:                     async with db.execute(\\n76:                         \\\"SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_consolidation_run'\\\"\\n77:                     ) as cursor:\\n78:                         row = await cursor.fetchone()\\n79:                 if row and row[0]:\\n80:                     last_run = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\\n81:                     if (now - last_run) > timedelta(hours=25):\\n82:                         events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n83:                             trigger=\\\"consolidation_stale\\\",\\n84:                             message=\\\"Consolidation has not run in 25h. Redis working memory may be stale.\\\",\\n85:                             priority=2,\\n86:                             expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=4),\\n87:                         ))\\n88:             except Exception as e:\\n89:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 2 (consolidation) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n90: \\n91:         if self._http is not None:\\n92:             try:\\n93:                 resp = await self._http.get(\\\"http://i9-node:8000/health\\\")\\n94:                 if resp.status_code != 200:\\n95:                     events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n96:                         trigger=\\\"inference_down\\\",\\n97:                         message=\\\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\\\",\\n98:                         priority=5,\\n99:                         expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\\n100:                     ))\\n101:             except Exception:\\n102:                 events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n103:                     trigger=\\\"inference_down\\\",\\n104:                     message=\\\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\\\",\\n105:                     priority=5,\\n106:                     expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\\n107:                 ))\\n108: \\n109:         if db_path is not None:\\n110:             try:\\n111:                 import aiosqlite\\n112:                 async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\\n113:                     async with db.execute(\\n114:                         \\\"SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_extraction_run'\\\"\\n115:                     ) as cursor:\\n116:                         row = await cursor.fetchone()\\n117:                 if row and row[0]:\\n118:                     last_extract = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\\n119:                     if (now - last_extract) > timedelta(hours=7):\\n120:                         events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n121:                             trigger=\\\"learning_loop_silence\\\",\\n122:                             message=\\\"Pattern extractor has been silent for 7h. Check xnch-core logs.\\\",\\n123:                             priority=4,\\n124:                             expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\\n125:                         ))\\n126:             except Exception as e:\\n127:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 4 (learning silence) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n128: \\n129:         for ev in events:\\n130:             await self.queue_event(ev)\\n131: \\n132:         return events\\n133: \\n134:     async def queue_event(self, event: ProactivityEvent) -> None:\\n135:         key = f\\\"proactivity:pending:{uuid4()}\\\"\\n136:         ttl_seconds = max(60, int((event.expires_at - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()))\\n137:         await self._redis.set(key, json.dumps(event.to_dict()), ex=ttl_seconds)\\n138: \\n139:     async def get_pending(self) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\\n140:         events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\\n141:         cursor = 0\\n142:         while True:\\n143:             cursor, keys = await self._redis.scan(cursor=cursor, match=\\\"proactivity:pending:*\\\")\\n144:             for k in keys:\\n145:                 raw = await self._redis.get(k)\\n146:                 if raw is None:\\n147:                     continue\\n148:                 try:\\n149:                     ev = ProactivityEvent.from_dict(json.loads(raw))\\n150:                     if not ev.expired:\\n151:                         events.append(ev)\\n152:                 except Exception:\\n153:                     pass\\n154:             if cursor == 0:\\n155:                 break\\n156:         events.sort(key=lambda e: e.priority, reverse=True)\\n157:         return events\\n\\n(End of file - total 157 lines)\\n</content>\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:37.067Z\",\"toolInput\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py\\\"}\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"toolOutput\":\"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/proactivity/engine.py</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: from __future__ import annotations\\n2: \\n3: import json\\n4: import logging\\n5: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\\n6: from datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\\n7: from uuid import uuid4\\n8: \\n9: logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n10: \\n11: \\n12: @dataclass\\n13: class ProactivityEvent:\\n14:     trigger: str\\n15:     message: str\\n16:     priority: int = 0\\n17:     expires_at: datetime = field(default_factory=lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc) + timedelta(hours=2))\\n18: \\n19:     @property\\n20:     def expired(self) -> bool:\\n21:         return datetime.now(timezone.utc) > self.expires_at\\n22: \\n23:     def to_dict(self) -> dict:\\n24:         return {\\n25:             \\\"trigger\\\": self.trigger,\\n26:             \\\"message\\\": self.message,\\n27:             \\\"priority\\\": self.priority,\\n28:             \\\"expires_at\\\": self.expires_at.isoformat(),\\n29:         }\\n30: \\n31:     @classmethod\\n32:     def from_dict(cls, d: dict) -> ProactivityEvent:\\n33:         return cls(\\n34:             trigger=d[\\\"trigger\\\"],\\n35:             message=d[\\\"message\\\"],\\n36:             priority=d.get(\\\"priority\\\", 0),\\n37:             expires_at=datetime.fromisoformat(d[\\\"expires_at\\\"]),\\n38:         )\\n39: \\n40: \\n41: class ProactivityEngine:\\n42:     def __init__(self, redis_client, http_client=None):\\n43:         self._redis = redis_client\\n44:         self._http = http_client\\n45: \\n46:     async def check_and_queue(\\n47:         self,\\n48:         pattern_store=None,\\n49:         db_path=None,\\n50:     ) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\\n51:         events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\\n52:         now = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\\n53: \\n54:         if pattern_store is not None:\\n55:             try:\\n56:                 patterns = await pattern_store.fetch_low_success(max_success_rate=0.4, min_confidence=0.5)\\n57:                 for p in patterns:\\n58:                     events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n59:                         trigger=\\\"stale_pattern\\\",\\n60:                         message=(\\n61:                             f\\\"ck-san, the {p.get('action_type', 'unknown')} pattern for \\\"\\n62:                             f\\\"{p.get('intent_class', 'unknown')} is failing 60%+ of the time. \\\"\\n63:                             f\\\"Want me to draft a policy candidate fix?\\\"\\n64:                         ),\\n65:                         priority=3,\\n66:                         expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\\n67:                     ))\\n68:             except Exception as e:\\n69:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 1 (stale pattern) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n70: \\n71:         if db_path is not None:\\n72:             try:\\n73:                 import aiosqlite\\n74:                 async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\\n75:                     async with db.execute(\\n76:                         \\\"SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_consolidation_run'\\\"\\n77:                     ) as cursor:\\n78:                         row = await cursor.fetchone()\\n79:                 if row and row[0]:\\n80:                     last_run = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\\n81:                     if (now - last_run) > timedelta(hours=25):\\n82:                         events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n83:                             trigger=\\\"consolidation_stale\\\",\\n84:                             message=\\\"Consolidation has not run in 25h. Redis working memory may be stale.\\\",\\n85:                             priority=2,\\n86:                             expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=4),\\n87:                         ))\\n88:             except Exception as e:\\n89:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 2 (consolidation) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n90: \\n91:         if self._http is not None:\\n92:             try:\\n93:                 resp = await self._http.get(\\\"http://i9-node:8000/health\\\")\\n94:                 if resp.status_code != 200:\\n95:                     events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n96:                         trigger=\\\"inference_down\\\",\\n97:                         message=\\\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\\\",\\n98:                         priority=5,\\n99:                         expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\\n100:                     ))\\n101:             except Exception:\\n102:                 events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n103:                     trigger=\\\"inference_down\\\",\\n104:                     message=\\\"Gemma 4 on i9 is not responding. Routing fallback to claude-judgment is active.\\\",\\n105:                     priority=5,\\n106:                     expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=1),\\n107:                 ))\\n108: \\n109:         if db_path is not None:\\n110:             try:\\n111:                 import aiosqlite\\n112:                 async with aiosqlite.connect(db_path) as db:\\n113:                     async with db.execute(\\n114:                         \\\"SELECT value FROM system_state WHERE key = 'last_extraction_run'\\\"\\n115:                     ) as cursor:\\n116:                         row = await cursor.fetchone()\\n117:                 if row and row[0]:\\n118:                     last_extract = datetime.fromisoformat(row[0])\\n119:                     if (now - last_extract) > timedelta(hours=7):\\n120:                         events.append(ProactivityEvent(\\n121:                             trigger=\\\"learning_loop_silence\\\",\\n122:                             message=\\\"Pattern extractor has been silent for 7h. Check xnch-core logs.\\\",\\n123:                             priority=4,\\n124:                             expires_at=now + timedelta(hours=2),\\n125:                         ))\\n126:             except Exception as e:\\n127:                 logger.warning(\\\"Proactivity Rule 4 (learning silence) failed: %s\\\", e)\\n128: \\n129:         for ev in events:\\n130:             await self.queue_event(ev)\\n131: \\n132:         return events\\n133: \\n134:     async def queue_event(self, event: ProactivityEvent) -> None:\\n135:         key = f\\\"proactivity:pending:{uuid4()}\\\"\\n136:         ttl_seconds = max(60, int((event.expires_at - datetime.now(timezone.utc)).total_seconds()))\\n137:         await self._redis.set(key, json.dumps(event.to_dict()), ex=ttl_seconds)\\n138: \\n139:     async def get_pending(self) -> list[ProactivityEvent]:\\n140:         events: list[ProactivityEvent] = []\\n141:         cursor = 0\\n142:         while True:\\n143:             cursor, keys = await self._redis.scan(cursor=cursor, match=\\\"proactivity:pending:*\\\")\\n144:             for k in keys:\\n145:                 raw = await self._redis.get(k)\\n146:                 if raw is None:\\n147:                     continue\\n148:                 try:\\n149:                     ev = ProactivityEvent.from_dict(json.loads(raw))\\n150:                     if not ev.expired:\\n151:                         events.append(ev)\\n152:                 except Exception:\\n153:                     pass\\n154:             if cursor == 0:\\n155:                 break\\n156:         events.sort(key=lambda e: e.priority, reverse=True)\\n157:         return events\\n\\n(End of file - total 157 lines)\\n</content>\"},\"type\":\"raw\"},\"obs_mqv8p901_120fa263fd11\":{\"observation\":{\"hookType\":\"post_tool_use\",\"id\":\"obs_mqv8p901_120fa263fd11\",\"raw\":{\"attachments\":[],\"call_id\":\"call_01_nBL6M718eEzoDabiEWVS3689\",\"duration_ms\":4,\"metadata\":{\"loaded\":[],\"preview\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Nexi v0 — decision engine FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport asyncio\\nimport logging\\nfrom contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\nfrom typing import Any\\nfrom uuid import UUID, uuid4\\n\\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, BackgroundTasks\\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse\\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\\n\\nfrom .adapters import XnchClient, ModelAdapter\\nfrom .config import settings\\nfrom .models import SessionContext\\nfrom .pipeline import (\\n    IntentInterpreter, ClarificationRequired,\\n    load_context,\\n    generate_options,\\n    PolicyFilter, AllOptionsBlocked,\\n    Evaluator,\",\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"nexi/nexi/main.py\",\"tool_input\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py\\\"}\",\"tool_name\":\"read\",\"tool_output\":\"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Nexi v0 — decision engine FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n2: import asyncio\\n3: import logging\\n4: from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\n5: from typing import Any\\n6: from uuid import UUID, uuid4\\n7: \\n8: from fastapi import FastAPI, HTTPException, BackgroundTasks\\n9: from fastapi.responses import JSONResponse as JSONResponse\\n10: from pydantic import BaseModel\\n11: \\n12: from .adapters import XnchClient, ModelAdapter\\n13: from .config import settings\\n14: from .models import SessionContext\\n15: from .pipeline import (\\n16:     IntentInterpreter, ClarificationRequired,\\n17:     load_context,\\n18:     generate_options,\\n19:     PolicyFilter, AllOptionsBlocked,\\n20:     Evaluator,\\n21:     select_decision,\\n22:     compile_action_spec, PlanCompilationError,\\n23:     dispatch_execution,\\n24: )\\n25: from .pipeline.dispatch import TokenExpired\\n26: from .utils.audit import emit_event\\n27: \\n28: logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\\n29: \\n30: \\n31: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n32: # App lifecycle\\n33: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n34: \\n35: _xnch: XnchClient | None = None\\n36: _model_adapter: ModelAdapter | None = None\\n37: _policy_filter: PolicyFilter | None = None\\n38: _intent_interpreter: IntentInterpreter | None = None\\n39: \\n40: \\n41: @asynccontextmanager\\n42: async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):\\n43:     global _xnch, _model_adapter, _policy_filter, _intent_interpreter\\n44:     _xnch = XnchClient()\\n45:     _model_adapter = ModelAdapter()\\n46:     _policy_filter = PolicyFilter(_xnch)\\n47:     _intent_interpreter = IntentInterpreter()\\n48:     yield\\n49:     await _xnch.aclose()\\n50: \\n51: \\n52: app = FastAPI(title=\\\"Nexi\\\", version=\\\"0.1.0\\\", lifespan=lifespan)\\n53: \\n54: \\n55: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n56: # Request / response schemas\\n57: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n58: \\n59: class SessionStartRequest(BaseModel):\\n60:     session_id: UUID\\n61:     trace_id: UUID\\n62:     actor: dict[str, Any]\\n63:     system_state_version: str\\n64:     policy_version: str\\n65:     raw_input: str\\n66:     priority: str = \\\"NORMAL\\\"\\n67:     idempotency_key: UUID\\n68: \\n69: \\n70: class SessionStartResponse(BaseModel):\\n71:     status: str\\n72:     decision_id: UUID | None = None\\n73:     execution_ref: UUID | None = None\\n74:     estimated_completion_ms: int | None = None\\n75:     audit_ref: UUID | None = None\\n76:     clarification_required: bool = False\\n77:     hold_id: UUID | None = None\\n78:     error: str | None = None\\n79: \\n80: \\n81: class ClarifyRequest(BaseModel):\\n82:     amended_input: str\\n83: \\n84: \\n85: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n86: # Endpoints\\n87: # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n88: \\n89: @app.post(\\\"/session/start\\\", response_model=SessionStartResponse)\\n90: async def session_start(\\n91:     body: SessionStartRequest,\\n92:     background_tasks: BackgroundTasks,\\n93: ) -> SessionStartResponse:\\n94:     \\\"\\\"\\\"Entry point called by xnch after actor resolution (Step 2 → Step 3).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n95:     session = SessionContext.model_validate(body.model_dump())\\n96:     emit_event(session.trace_id, \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"SESSION_START_RECEIVED\\\",\\n97:                {\\\"session_id\\\": str(session.session_id)})\\n98: \\n99:     if _intent_interpreter is None:\\n100:         return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ERROR\\\", error=\\\"intent interpreter not available\\\")\\n101: \\n102:     # Step 3 — Intent interpretation\\n103:     try:\\n104:         intent = await _intent_interpreter.interpret(\\n105:             body.raw_input, session.session_id, str(session.trace_id)\\n106:         )\\n107:     except ClarificationRequired as exc:\\n108:         return SessionStartResponse(\\n109:             status=\\\"CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED\\\",\\n110:             clarification_required=True,\\n111:         )\\n112: \\n113:     # Step 4 — Context manifest (hard stop on failure)\\n114:     try:\\n115:         manifest = await load_context(_xnch, session, intent)\\n116:     except Exception as exc:\\n117:         logger.error(\\\"Context manifest load failed: %s\\\", exc)\\n118:         raise HTTPException(status_code=503, detail=\\\"DEGRADED: context manifest unavailable\\\")\\n119: \\n120:     # Fetch weight config for this intent class (cached per session)\\n121:     try:\\n122:         weight_config = await _xnch.get_weight_config(intent.intent_class)\\n123:     except Exception:\\n124:         weight_config = None\\n125: \\n126:     evaluator = Evaluator(weight_config)\\n127: \\n128:     # Step 5 — Option generation\\n129:     n = settings.options_count\\n130:     raw_options, generation_path = await generate_options(\\n131:         _model_adapter, session, intent, manifest, n\\n132:     )\\n133: \\n134:     # Step 6 — Policy alignment filter\\n135:     try:\\n136:         surviving = await _policy_filter.filter(session, raw_options)\\n137:     except AllOptionsBlocked:\\n138:         hold_id = uuid4()\\n139:         emit_event(str(session.trace_id), \\\"nexi\\\", \\\"ESCALATED_ALL_BLOCKED\\\",\\n140:                    {\\\"hold_id\\\": str(hold_id)})\\n141:         return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n142: \\n143:     # Step 7 — Scoring\\n144:     evaluated = evaluator.score(surviving, intent, manifest, session)\\n145: \\n146:     # Step 8 — Outcome simulation (conditional)\\n147:     evaluated = evaluator.simulate_and_rescore(evaluated, surviving, manifest, intent, session)\\n148: \\n149:     # Step 9 — Selection\\n150:     n_blocked = len(raw_options) - len(surviving)\\n151:     decision = select_decision(\\n152:         session, intent, manifest,\\n153:         [opt for opt, _ in surviving], evaluated,\\n154:         n_generated=len(raw_options),\\n155:         n_blocked=n_blocked,\\n156:         generation_path=generation_path,\\n157:     )\\n158: \\n159:     if decision.escalation_triggered:\\n160:         hold_id = uuid4()\\n161:         return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n162: \\n163:     # Step 10a — Plan compilation\\n164:     selected_opt = next(\\n165:         (opt for opt, _ in surviving if opt.option_id == decision.selected_option_id),\\n166:         None,\\n167:     )\\n168:     if selected_opt is None:\\n169:         raise HTTPException(status_code=500, detail=\\\"Selected option not found\\\")\\n170: \\n171:     try:\\n172:         compiled = compile_action_spec(selected_opt)\\n173:     except PlanCompilationError as exc:\\n174:         raise HTTPException(status_code=422, detail=str(exc))\\n175: \\n176:     if not compiled.nodes:\\n177:         return JSONResponse({'error': 'compiled DAG has no nodes'}, status_code=422)\\n178:     node = compiled.nodes[0]\\n179:     validated_action_spec = {\\n180:         \\\"type\\\": node.action_type,\\n181:         \\\"target\\\": node.target,\\n182:         \\\"params\\\": node.params,\\n183:     }\\n184: \\n185:     # Step 10 — Final verdict\\n186:     try:\\n187:         verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n188:             session, decision, validated_action_spec, selected_opt.payload_hash\\n189:         )\\n190:     except Exception as exc:\\n191:         error_body = str(exc)\\n192:         if \\\"STALE_SESSION\\\" in error_body:\\n193:             raise HTTPException(status_code=409, detail=\\\"STALE_SESSION: restart required\\\")\\n194:         raise HTTPException(status_code=502, detail=f\\\"Verdict submission failed: {error_body}\\\")\\n195: \\n196:     if verdict.verdict == \\\"BLOCK\\\":\\n197:         hold_id = uuid4()\\n198:         return SessionStartResponse(status=\\\"ESCALATED\\\", hold_id=hold_id)\\n199: \\n200:     # Step 11 — Execution dispatch (async handoff)\\n201:     execution_runner_url = settings.execution_runner_url\\n202:     try:\\n203:         dispatch_payload = await dispatch_execution(\\n204:             session, decision, verdict, validated_action_spec, execution_runner_url\\n205:         )\\n206:     except TokenExpired:\\n207:         # Resubmit to xnch for a new token, same decision_id\\n208:         verdict = await _xnch.submit_verdict(\\n209:             session, decision, vali\"},\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fae6128fffeZVZEUxWHD6wrvY\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:03:37.295Z\",\"toolInput\":\"{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py\\\"}\",\"toolName\":\"read\",\"toolOutput\":\"<path>/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/main.py</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Nexi v0 — decision engine FastAPI application.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n2: import asyncio\\n3: import logging\\n4: from contextlib import asynccontextmanager\\n5: from typing import Any\\n6: from uuid import UUID, uuid4\\n7: \\n8: from fastapi import FastA