nchSystems/deploy/docker/nexi.Dockerfile\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8anyx_485410216522\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The Dockerfile for the Nexi service was read to understand the build environment and runtime configuration. This provides details on the Python version, dependency management via uv/pip, and the application entry point.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting the containerization configuration for the Nexi application\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:16.856Z\",\"title\":\"Read Dockerfile for Nexi service\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8ao5q_a3aa74227674\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Kubernetes CronJob\",\"Python asyncio\",\"K8s job scheduling\",\"Postgres connection strings\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"CronJob name: consolidation\",\"Namespace: xnch-system\",\"Schedule: 0 2 * * * (daily at 02:00)\",\"Container image: xnch/xnch-server:latest\",\"Execution command: python -c \\\"import asyncio; from xnch.jobs.consolidation import run_consolidation; asyncio.run(run_consolidation())\\\"\",\"Environment variable XNCH_POSTGRES_URL uses $(POSTGRES_PASSWORD) secret placeholder\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/k8s/jobs/consolidation-cronjob.yaml\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ao5q_a3aa74227674\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The system read the Kubernetes CronJob definition for the consolidation task. This job runs a Python script within the xnch-server container on a daily schedule to perform data consolidation tasks.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining Kubernetes CronJob configuration for consolidation task\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:17.101Z\",\"title\":\"Read consolidation CronJob manifest\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8aqzt_6072696884bd\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Kubernetes Deployment\",\"Kubernetes Service\",\"K8s Resource Limits\",\"NodeSelector\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Deployment name is 'xnch' in namespace 'xnch-system'\",\"Uses Recreate deployment strategy\",\"Container runs on nodes with role: memory\",\"Requires Redis and PostgreSQL (pgvector) connections\",\"Resource limits: 1.5Gi memory, 1 CPU; requests: 768Mi memory, 500m CPU\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/k8s/i7-node/xnch-deployment.yaml\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8aqzt_6072696884bd\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the Kubernetes deployment and service manifest for the xnch application. The configuration defines the core deployment parameters, environment variables, and volume mounts for the xnch-server.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining xnch-deployment.yaml for service architecture\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:20.775Z\",\"title\":\"Read Kubernetes deployment configuration\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8atxe_fe33a2d415ed\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LLM classification\",\"LiteLLM proxy\",\"Async HTTP requests\",\"Intent parsing\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The `_classify_with_llm` method uses httpx to call a LiteLLM proxy.\",\"It uses the \\\"phi3-encoder\\\" model for classification.\",\"The request uses a system prompt and raw input to generate a JSON object response.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8atxe_fe33a2d415ed\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"Examined the implementation of the intent classification method within the pipeline. This code handles sending raw user input to an LLM endpoint to determine the user's intent.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting LLM classification logic in intent_interpreter.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:24.575Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8au28_2ccb4746896e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\",\"Python decorators\",\"FastAPI middleware logic\",\"Trust hierarchy\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"TrustLevel enum defines hierarchy: UNTRUSTED (1) to SYSTEM (5).\",\"ACTOR_TRUST_mapping assigns specific roles (nexi, openclaw, etc.) to trust levels.\",\"@requires_trust decorator enforces minimum trust levels by checking 'X-Actor-Role' header in FastAPI requests.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8au28_2ccb4746896e\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"Read the security trust model implementation to understand how actor permissions are enforced within the system. This file defines the core authorization logic based on actor identity.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examination of trust level hierarchy and access control logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:24.750Z\",\"title\":\"Read security trust model definition\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8aubq_112a90f2e197\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"policy DSL\",\"LLM-driven governance\",\"pattern-based rule generation\",\"SQLite persistence\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Module implements an LLM-driven policy rule proposal system.\",\"Reads low-success, high-confidence patterns from PatternStore.\",\"Uses LiteLLM proxy at http://localhost:4000/v1/chat/completions.\",\"Outputs policy rules with ALLOW/BLOCK/MODIFY/DEFER verdicts to SQLite.\",\"Uses 'claude-judgment' model.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8aubq_112a90f2e197\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The file contains the logic for generating new policy candidates based on identified patterns. This is a core component of the autonomous governance loop.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining the Policy Candidate Generator implementation\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:25.091Z\",\"title\":\"Read policy_candidates.py module\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8auiv_405cd7293f76\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"data seeding\",\"episodic memory\",\"identity management\",\"PgEpisodicStore\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"IDENTITY_FACTS contains core identity traits for 'ck-san'\",\"ck-san is a Senior Platform Engineer at Rakuten India\",\"XNCH is the orchestration platform; Nexi is the product interface layer\",\"Local setup uses Gemma 4 26B on RTX 3090\",\"seed_identity_memories function populates PgEpisodicStore\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8auiv_405cd7293f76\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Read the cold start seeder script to understand the foundational identity facts being injected into the episodic memory store. This script ensures the agent starts with the correct persona and technical context.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting cold start seed data for character identity\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:25.349Z\",\"title\":\"Read identity seeding script\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8ax9x_e98842d178d2\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"regex-based intent classification\",\"entity extraction\",\"NLP pipeline\",\"intent classification\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Uses regex patterns in _RULES to map input to IntentClass (DECISION, ESCALATION, etc.)\",\"_rule_classify function iterates through compiled regex patterns to determine intent\",\"_extract_entity function performs basic tokenization to identify entity IDs and types (ML_MODEL, SERVICE, DATABASE, etc.)\",\"Identifies resource types like CLUSTER, FILE, SCRIPT, and SCHEMA based on keyword hints\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ax9x_e98842d178d2\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Examined the core logic of the intent interpreter pipeline. This reveals how user inputs are parsed into structured intents and how entities are extracted from raw text strings.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting intent classification rules and extraction logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:28.915Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8axl5_875e3e675099\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"rule-based action triggering\",\"user idle detection\",\"asynchronous task scheduling\",\"background consolidation\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The filter triggers a 'trigger_file_watcher' action when a vault file is saved.\",\"The filter triggers 'suppress_responses_and_consolidate' when user idle duration exceeds a timeout.\",\"Idle timeout triggers an asynchronous consolidation job via 'run_consolidation'.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/perception/attention_filter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8axl5_875e3e675099\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The file contains logic for evaluating rules to determine system actions. It specifically handles file watcher triggers and automated consolidation tasks based on user activity levels.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting rule-based action triggering in perception module\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:29.319Z\",\"title\":\"Read attention_filter.py logic\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8axyj_57577f52e77b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"prompt injection prevention\",\"regex security filters\",\"negative lookahead\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"File: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\",\"Contains regex patterns for detecting prompt injection attempts\",\"Pattern 1: 'disregard...above' (case-insensitive)\",\"Pattern 2: 'act as (?!Nexi)' (negative lookahead to prevent persona hijacking)\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8axyj_57577f52e77b\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The engine inspected specific lines of the injection guard security module. These regex patterns are designed to detect common prompt injection techniques like instruction overriding and persona impersonation.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting security filters in injection_guard.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:29.802Z\",\"title\":\"Read injection guard regex patterns\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8b6zf_478d300b9b96\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"async/await\",\"httpx AsyncClient\",\"Observability client refactoring\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed self._client from httpx.Client to httpx.AsyncClient\",\"Replaced close() method with async aclose() method\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/observability/langfuse_client.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8b6zf_478d300b9b96\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The LangfuseClient was updated to use an asynchronous HTTP client (httpx.AsyncClient) to support non-blocking I/O operations. This change prepares the observability client for async-compatible workflows.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Migrating from synchronous httpx.Client to httpx.AsyncClient\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:41.497Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor LangfuseClient to use AsyncClient\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8b7gt_6d182976e2f8\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"audio signal processing\",\"numpy buffer conversion\",\"PCM normalization\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed input dtype from np.float32 to np.int16\",\"Added normalization by dividing by 32768.0 to scale int16 range to [-1.0, 1.0]\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/perception/voice_daemon.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8b7gt_6d182976e2f8\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The audio buffer was incorrectly being read as float32. This change ensures the raw buffer is read as int16 and then normalized to float32 for consistent processing.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Corrected buffer interpretation from float32 to int16 before normalization\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:42.122Z\",\"title\":\"Fix audio buffer dtype conversion in voice_daemon.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8b8h6_41bdbec8f6a6\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Docker layer caching\",\"Python runtime upgrade\",\"Multi-stage build optimization\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Updated base image from python:3.11-slim to python:3.13-slim\",\"Reordered COPY instructions to copy pyproject.toml before the full directory to improve layer caching\",\"Removed redundant COPY nexi/ before pyproject.toml in the new version\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/docker/nexi.Dockerfile\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8b8h6_41bdbec8f6a6\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The Dockerfile was updated to use a newer Python runtime and optimize build caching by placing dependency files earlier in the layer sequence. This reduces rebuild time when only source code changes.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Upgrading Python version and restructuring Dockerfile layers\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:43.432Z\",\"title\":\"Update Docker base image and optimize COPY layers\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8b8zp_4fc8ffd95f50\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Kubernetes secrets\",\"environment variable refactoring\",\"secure credential management\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Modified /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/k8s/jobs/consolidation-cronjob.yaml\",\"Replaced hardcoded POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable with secretKeyRef from xnch-secret\",\"Maintained XNCH_POSTGRES_URL using the updated POSTGRES_PASSWORD variable\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/k8s/jobs/consolidation-cronjob.yaml\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8b8zp_4fc8ffd95f50\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"The deployment configuration was updated to use a Kubernetes secret for the database password instead of relying on an-injected environment variable. This improves security by following best practices for credential management in K8s.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Migrate XNCH_POSTGRES_URL from plain text variable to Kubernetes secret reference\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:44.099Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor postgres password retrieval in cronjob\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8ba0r_b0a65006c462\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Kubernetes Secrets\",\"Environment Variable Refactoring\",\"K8s deployment configuration\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Replaced hardcoded POSTGRES_PASSWORD environment variable with valueFrom SecretKeyRef\",\"Source secret name: xnch-secret\",\"Secret key: postgres_password\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/deploy/k8s/i7-node/xnch-deployment.yaml\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8ba0r_b0a65006c462\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"Modified the Kubernetes deployment configuration to improve security by fetching the PostgreSQL password from a Kubernetes Secret instead of using a potentially plaintext environment variable. This change ensures credentials are managed via the K8s secret store.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Updating xnch-deployment.yaml to use SecretKeyRef for database credentials\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:45.431Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor Postgres password retrieval in K8s deployment\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bakx_f1b4f7b68ce7\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"string parsing\",\"tokenization\",\"intent interpretation\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed entity_id extraction from single token (tokens[1]) to a joined string of all remaining tokens (tokens[1:])\",\"This allows for multi-word entity identifiers in the input string\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bakx_f1b4f7b68ce7\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The parsing logic in intent_interpreter.py was updated to handle entity IDs that contain spaces. Previously, only the first token after the command was captured; now, all subsequent tokens are joined into a single entity_id string.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Modified entity_id extraction logic in intent_interpreter.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:46.159Z\",\"title\":\"Update intent interpreter token parsing\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bb0c_9907c36303cf\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LLM configuration\",\"model switching\",\"intent interpreter\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed model configuration from 'phi3-encoder' to 'gemma4-local' in /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bb0c_9907c36303cf\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The model configuration within the intent interpreter pipeline was updated to use the gemma4-local model instead of phi3-encoder. This change likely reflects an upgrade or shift in the underlying LLM architecture being used for intent processing.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Swapping phi3-encoder for gemma4-local\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:46.714Z\",\"title\":\"Update model identifier in intent_interpreter.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bbr1_1bdf406d1861\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"type safety\",\"Python type checking\",\"duck typing\",\"middleware security\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Modified /Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py\",\"Replaced hasattr(arg, 'headers') check with isinstance(arg, Request) check\",\"Updated logic for both positional args and keyword kwargs\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/security/trust_model.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bbr1_1bdf406d1861\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Refactored the way the trust model identifies the Request object within function arguments. This moves from a duck-typing approach to explicit type checking with the Request class, improving type safety and predictability.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Switch from duck-typing (hasattr) to explicit type checking (isinstance) for Request objects\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:47.675Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor request extraction logic in trust_model.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bcxa_84c4171434c8\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"environment configuration\",\"dynamic configuration\",\"liteLLM proxy\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed _LLM_URL from a hardcoded localhost address to a conditional check using settings.litellm_proxy_url\",\"Fallback URL is set to http://litellm:4000/v1/chat/completions if setting is missing\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bcxa_84c4171434c8\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The code was updated to allow for more flexible LLM endpoint configuration via a settings object. This allows the system to transition from local development defaults to a service-based proxy URL.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Refactoring _LLM_URL in policy_candidates.py to support configurable liteLLM proxy URL\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:49.195Z\",\"title\":\"Update LLM URL to use dynamic settings\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bfma_06f1686a7727\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Pydantic Settings\",\"Environment configuration\",\"System architecture paths\",\"Observability (Langfuse)\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Application base directory is ~/.xnch\",\"Uses Pydantic Settings with XNCH_ environment prefix\",\"Config defines paths for keys, audit, governance, policies, and weights\",\"Includes Redis, PostgreSQL (pgvector), and Langfuse observability settings\",\"Contains perception-related thresholds for attention and silence detection\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/config.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bfma_06f1686a7727\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The file was read to understand the global application configuration, including directory structures, database URLs, and runtime thresholds for the perception engine.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting Settings class in config.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:52.689Z\",\"title\":\"Read application configuration\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bix2_2a67b73c90fa\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LiteLLM proxy\",\"model configuration\",\"LLM orchestration\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Added `litellm_proxy_url` set to \\\"http://litellm:4000\\\"\",\"Added `graph_extractor_model` set to \\\"ollama/phi3:mini\\\"\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/config.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bix2_2a67b73c90fa\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Modified the configuration file to include proxy URL and specific model identifier for the graph extractor component. This enables integration with LiteLLM and specifies the local Ollama model to use.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Configuring LiteLLM proxy and model paths in configuration\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:52:56.964Z\",\"title\":\"Update config.py with LiteLLM and Graph Extractor settings\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8blf8_2d29023444e8\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"LLM proxy configuration\",\"LiteLLM integration\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"_LLM_URL is derived from settings.litellm_proxy_url or defaults to http://litellm:4000/v1/chat/completions\",\"The file belongs to the xnch learning module\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8blf8_2d29023444e8\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Read a snippet of policy_candidates.py to understand how LLM completion URLs are constructed. This is part of an investigation into where the litellm proxy configuration is defined.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting LLM endpoint configuration in learning module\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:53:00.209Z\",\"title\":\"Read policy_candidates.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8boet_3451722dcdd0\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"URL path manipulation\",\"Environment configuration\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py updated\",\"Removed conditional logic for litellm_proxy_url fallback\",\"Added .rstrip(\\\"/\\\") to settings.litellm_proxy_url to prevent double slashes\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/learning/policy_candidates.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8boet_3451722dcdd0\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The code was refactored to use a more robust string concatenation method for the LLM endpoint URL. This ensures that the URL remains valid regardless of whether the setting ends with a trailing slash.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Refactoring _LLM_URL to use rstrip for safer path joining\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:53:04.083Z\",\"title\":\"Update LLM URL construction in policy_candidates.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8bria_55285617160f\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[],\"confidence\":0.85,\"facts\":[\"Replaced manual iteration over episodic_store.list_recent with a targeted search_memory call\",\"Updated logic to use search_memory with filter_metadata for \\\"identity\\\" type\",\"Reduced complexity from O(N) scan to targeted retrieval\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/character/cold_start_seeder.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8bria_55285617160f\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The identity check in the cold start seeder was refactored to use the more efficient search_memory API. This optimizes 