-06-26T17:58:39.832Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8j07o_2f7ee78a0ba0\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"vector database upsert\",\"similarity threshold\",\"vector search filtering\",\"embedding management\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The `create_memory` function performs an upsert into a collection with metadata and embeddings.\",\"`create_unique_memory` checks for existing similar memories using a similarity threshold (default 0.95) before creating a new entry.\",\"The `search_memory` function supports distance-based filtering (min/max distance) and metadata filtering (e.g., 'novel' flag).\",\"Similarity is calculated using distance (max_distance = 1.0 - similarity).\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8j07o_2f7ee78a0ba0\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"The user inspected the implementation of the memory management system to understand how memories are created, searched, and deduplicated based on similarity thresholds.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Code review of memory creation and search logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:58:45.971Z\",\"title\":\"Inspecting agentmemory/main.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8j2md_9f24b07f4f39\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"python package inspection\",\"function signature discovery\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Function `get_memory(category, id, include_embeddings=True)` exists at line 189 of .venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py\"],\"files\":[\".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8j2md_9f24b07f4f39\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The user executed a grep command to locate the exact definition and line number of the `get_memory` function within the installed `agentmemory` package.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Locating function definition in site-packages\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:58:49.091Z\",\"title\":\"Search for get_memory definition in agentmemory\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8j4xk_32bff05d7f95\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"memory retrieval\",\"vector database collections\",\"embedding retrieval\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"get_memory(category, id, include_embeddings=True) retrieves specific memory by ID within a category.\",\"Uses get_client().get_or_create_collection(category) to access the relevant collection.\",\"Retrieval logic depends on get_include_types to determine if embeddings are fetched.\"],\"files\":[\".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8j4xk_32bff05d7f95\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the source code for the get_memory function to understand how the memory retrieval process handles category selection and embedding inclusion. This is critical for understanding the underlying data retrieval mechanism in the agent's memory system.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Reviewing memory retrieval logic in agentmemory/main.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:58:52.086Z\",\"title\":\"Inspect get_memory implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8j7b6_9e20bbf05aee\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"memory retrieval logic\",\"ChromaDB integration\",\"vector database querying\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The get_memory function retrieves specific memory IDs from a collection.\",\"Uses chroma_collection_to_list to process results.\",\"Includes logging for successful and failed memory retrieval attempts.\",\"Returns the first memory object if found, or None if the list is empty.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/main.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8j7b6_9e20bbf05aee\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"The user inspected the implementation details of the memory retrieval function within the agentmemory package. This reveals the logic used to fetch and validate individual memory entries from the vector database.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Reading lines 210-225 of the memory retrieval logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:58:55.168Z\",\"title\":\"Inspect agentmemory/main.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jajc_192f1764b719\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"episodic memory\",\"memory retrieval\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Modified /Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"Added 'get_memory' to the import list from 'agentmemory'\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jajc_192f1764b719\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Updated the imports in the episodic memory storage module to include the get_memory function. This allows the module to retrieve single memory entries in addition to existing search and list capabilities.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Added get_memory import to pg_episodic_store.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:58:59.350Z\",\"title\":\"Update imports in pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jd50_2e7ba04544df\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"python package exports\",\"module initialization\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"The string \\\"get_memory\\\" exists in .venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/__init__.py\"],\"files\":[\".venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/agentmemory/__init__.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jd50_2e7ba04544df\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Ran a grep command to confirm if get_memory is exported within the agentmemory package. The search returned a positive match, confirming the function is available in the package's init file.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying presence of get_memory in agentmemory package\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:02.722Z\",\"title\":\"Search for get_memory export\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jg31_39e1f1b84300\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"data access abstraction\",\"refactoring\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Replaced search_memory call with a direct get_memory call\",\"Removed manual filtering by id in the search parameters\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jg31_39e1f1b84300\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The method _get_memory_by_id was refactored to use a higher-level get_memory function instead of a manual search with filters, simplifying the implementation.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Simplified memory retrieval logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:06.539Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor _get_memory_by_id in pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jkxn_5796a683207e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"unit testing\",\"mocking\",\"API refactoring\",\"postgresql episodic store\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"Changed patch target from xnch.memory.pg_episodic_store.get_memories to xnch.memory.pg_episodic_store.get_memory\",\"Updated mock return value from a list of dictionaries to a single dictionary\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jkxn_5796a683207e\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The test suite was updated to align with a change in the episodic store API, moving from a plural memory retrieval method to a singular one. This ensures the unit test correctly mocks the single object return type.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Updated test case to reflect change from get_memories to get_memory\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:12.825Z\",\"title\":\"Refactor mock memory retrieval in pg_episodic_store tests\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jnmf_7a7a22ebf7c2\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"Python imports\",\"code refactoring\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py: removed search_memory from imports\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jnmf_7a7a22ebf7c2\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"Removed an unused 'search_memory' import from the agentmemory module within the pg_episodic_store.py file. This cleanup reduces unnecessary dependencies in the memory storage implementation.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Cleaning up imports in episodic memory storage module\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:16.309Z\",\"title\":\"Remove unused import in pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_edit\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8jvhh_cce47fe31c3a\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"unit testing\",\"NotImplementedError\",\"HMAC security\",\"integration testing\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"4 tests failed out of 194 total tests\",\"Failed tests: nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py (2 tests), xnch/tests/test_pg_episontic_store.py (2 tests)\",\"Identified NotImplementedError in xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"InsecureKeyLengthWarning: HMAC key is 29 bytes (min 32 required)\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\",\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8jvhh_cce47fe31c3a\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The full test suite was executed, revealing 4 failures and several warnings. Two failures are due to NotImplementedError in the episodic store and two are related to the intent interpreter, indicating regression or incomplete implementation in the persistence and interpretation layers.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"pytest execution in xnchSystems directory\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:26.497Z\",\"title\":\"Full test suite execution failure\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k09c_9aac7294080b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"NotImplementedError\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"API deprecation\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"test_execute failed with NotImplementedError\",\"test_fetchval failed with NotImplementedError\",\"The execute() and fetchval() methods in PgEpisodicStore are currently stubs that raise NotImplementedError\",\"The error message indicates a design decision to move away from direct SQL execution in favor of store_episode or agentmemory calls\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k09c_9aac7294080b\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Running pytest revealed that two tests in test_pg_episodic_store.py failed because the execute and fetchval methods in PgEpisodicStore have had their implementations removed in favor of higher-level APIs. This confirms the need to update the test suite or reimplement the required functionality.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running regression tests for PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:32.686Z\",\"title\":\"pytest failure in pg_episodic_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k1zx_cb338779dcf1\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"unit testing\",\"mocking async calls\",\"error handling fallback\",\"pytest\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"test_ambiguous_input_uses_llm failed: Expected _classify_with_llm to be awaited once, but it was awaited 0 times.\",\"test_llm_failure_falls_back failed: Expected ambiguity_score to be 0.5 on LLM failure, but got 0.0.\"],\"files\":[\"nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k1zx_cb338779dcf1\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"The pytest execution on the intent interpreter pipeline failed with two specific test regressions. One test failed to trigger the LLM classification path, and another failed to correctly assign a fallback ambiguity score when the LLM service fails.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running pytest on nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py reveals two assertion errors\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:34.939Z\",\"title\":\"pytest failures in intent_interpreter tests\",\"type\":\"error\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k6n4_c2e65b90505e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest async\",\"SQL integration testing\",\"mocking/patching\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests include test_execute for SQL UPDATE commands\",\"Tests include test_fetchval using patches for get_memories\",\"Tests include test_retrieve_similar_empty for handling empty results\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k6n4_c2e65b90505e\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"Read a segment of the episodic store test suite to understand the implementation of SQL execution and value fetching within the pg_episodic_store. This provides context for how the database interactions are validated.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspecting unit tests for PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:40.958Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8k6xx_841aa3235cc8\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"asyncio testing\",\"mocking\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"unit testing\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"File: /Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"Tests use pytest and unittest.mock to validate PgEpisodicStore\",\"Includes an async fixture for managing store connection/disconnection\",\"Uses a mock for the 'create_memory' function\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8k6xx_841aa3235cc8\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"The agent read the beginning of the test suite for the PostgreSQL episodic memory store. This file contains the core logic for testing episode creation and storage functionality within the xnch memory system.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining unit tests for PgEpisodicStore\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:41.347Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kapy_1a90c3f5981d\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"unit testing\",\"pg_episodic_store\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Command executed: pytest xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py with exclusions\",\"Two tests were deselected: test_execute and test_fetchval\",\"Test execution completed successfully in 0.45s\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kapy_1a90c3f5981d\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Ran a targeted pytest suite to ensure that tests other than the specific execution and fetchval tests pass in the pg_episodic_store module. This helps isolate regressions in the remaining test suite.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying remaining tests in test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:46.244Z\",\"title\":\"Run pytest on pg_episode_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kdu3_687fc5d0fe12\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"pytest\",\"PostgreSQL episodic store\",\"NotImplementedError\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests failed: 2 failed, 5 passed\",\"Errors caused by NotImplementedError in xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py:167\",\"Failed test cases: test_execute, test_fetchval\"],\"files\":[\"xnch/xnch/memory/pg_episodic_store.py\",\"xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kdu3_687fc5d0fe12\",\"importance\":6,\"narrative\":\"Running the pytest suite for the PostgreSQL episodic store revealed unimplemented methods in the implementation. This indicates that the core database interaction logic for execution and value fetching is missing.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Executing pytest on xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:50.282Z\",\"title\":\"Run pg_episodic_store tests\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"LiteLLM\",\"input injection guarding\",\"structured prompt engineering\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Uses LiteLLM for intent classification into QUERY, DECISION, EXECution, and ESCALATION.\",\"Implements a rule-based pre-filter stage before LLM processing.\",\"Includes security scanning via xnch.security.injection_guard.\",\"Defines a JSON schema for structured intent extraction including action_type, entity_class, and urgency.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the core intent classification module to understand how user inputs are parsed, validated for injections, and categorized into actionable intents. This is a critical component of the pipeline's decision-making logic.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Analyzing LiteLLM-backed intent classification logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.185Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"pytest fixture\",\"mocking async clients\",\"unit testing pipeline\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Tests cover IntentClass types: EXECUTION, QUERY, and ESCALATION.\",\"Uses pytest and unittest.mock to simulate LiteLLM responses.\",\"Includes tests for handling ambiguous inputs that trigger ClarificationRequired exceptions.\",\"Mocks httpx.AsyncClient to control LLM response simulation.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\",\"importance\":3,\"narrative\":\"Read the test suite for the intent interpreter to understand how the system handles different intent classifications and ambiguity levels. This provides context for the expected behavior of the LLM-driven intent parsing logic.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining unit tests for the IntentInterpreter pipeline component\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.486Z\",\"title\":\"Read test_intent_interpreter.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"regex-based parsing\",\"hybrid retrieval\",\"entity extraction\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"The system uses a two-stage approach: regex-based pre-filtering followed by memory-based recall.\",\"Regex rules map specific command prefixes (e.g., 'list', 'show', 'deploy') to IntentClasses (QUERY, EXECUTION, etc.).\",\"The `_rule_classify` function provides 1.0 confidence/0.0 ambiguity for regex matches.\",\"`_extract_entity` parses input to identify target entities like models, services, or databases.\",\"`_recall_intent` queries 'intent-classifications' memory to find previously matched intents.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Inspected the core intent parsing logic in the pipeline. The implementation uses a hybrid approach of deterministic regex rules and a vector/memory search for historical intents.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Examining the rule-based and memory-based intent classification logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T17:59:58.286Z\",\"title\":\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"prompt injection detection\",\"regex-based security scanning\",\"security auditing\",\"risk scoring\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"Uses regex patterns to detect common prompt injection strings (e.g., 'ignore previous instructions', 'DAN mode').\",\"Calculates a risk_score based on the proportion of matched patterns found.\",\"Integrates with EventLog to log security warnings when risk_score exceeds 0.1.\",\"Uses a dataclass InjectionResult to return scan results.\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\",\"importance\":4,\"narrative\":\"The file contains the implementation for scanning text inputs for potential prompt injection attacks. It uses a predefined list of regex patterns to identify malicious instructions and logs attempts via an EventLog system.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Inspection of prompt injection detection logic\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:06.730Z\",\"title\":\"Read security/injection_guard.py\",\"type\":\"file_read\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"unit testing\",\"intent classification\",\"mocking async methods\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"IntentInterpreter correctly mapped 'xyzzyplex frobnicate' to EXECUTION/DEPLOY intent class via mock\",\"Mocked _classify_with_llm was not called during the test execution\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Executed a standalone Python script to verify if IntentInterpreter correctly processes input. The test showed the expected intent class and action type but revealed the LLM mock was not triggered as expected, suggesting a potential issue in the interpretation flow or method interception.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Running unit test for IntentInterpreter with mocked LLM\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:18.594Z\",\"title\":\"Verify IntentInterpreter classification logic\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"intent classification\",\"rule-based engine\",\"unit testing\",\"mocking\"],\"confidence\":1,\"facts\":[\"_rule_classify returned None for input 'xyzzyplex frobnicate'\",\"_recall_intent successfully identified an EXECUTION intent with DEPLOY action\",\"LLM classification was bypassed via mock, confirming-rule-based logic paths\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\",\"importance\":5,\"narrative\":\"Ran a standalone Python test script to debug the internal components of IntentInterpreter. The test verified that rule-based classification failed for the dummy string, but the recall mechanism successfully identified a high-urgency deployment intent.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying rule-based classification and intent recall\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:29.395Z\",\"title\":\"Debug intent interpreter logic via python script\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8lfsf_d4273e7e117e\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"ChromaDB\",\"persistent storage\",\"vector database\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"facts\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/memory/ directory does not exist\"],\"files\":[\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/memory/\"],\"id\":\"obs_mqv8lfsf_d4273e7e117e\",\"importance\":2,\"narrative\":\"The system attempted to locate the ChromaDB persistent storage directory to check for existing memory. The directory was not found, indicating no persistent vector database has been initialized at this path.\",\"sessionId\":\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\",\"subtitle\":\"Verifying existence of persistent storage\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-06-26T18:00:39.470Z\",\"title\":\"Check for ChromaDB memory directory\",\"type\":\"command_run\"},\"type\":\"compressed\"},\"obs_mqv8lm9g_1e59d319d634\":{\"observation\":{\"concepts\":[\"python source code search\"