":6,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Running the pytest suite for the PostgreSQL episodic store revealed unimplemented methods in the implementation. This indicates that the core database interaction logic for execution and value fetching is missing.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Executing pytest on xnch/tests/test_pg_episodic_store.py\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T17:59:50.282Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Run pg_episodic_store tests\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_run\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"intent classification\\\",\\\"LiteLLM\\\",\\\"input injection guarding\\\",\\\"structured prompt engineering\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":1,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"Uses LiteLLM for intent classification into QUERY, DECISION, EXECution, and ESCALATION.\\\",\\\"Implements a rule-based pre-filter stage before LLM processing.\\\",\\\"Includes security scanning via xnch.security.injection_guard.\\\",\\\"Defines a JSON schema for structured intent extraction including action_type, entity_class, and urgency.\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8kguj_e947cbb58588\\\",\\\"importance\\\":5,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Inspected the core intent classification module to understand how user inputs are parsed, validated for injections, and categorized into actionable intents. This is a critical component of the pipeline's decision-making logic.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Analyzing LiteLLM-backed intent classification logic\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.185Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_read\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"intent classification\\\",\\\"pytest fixture\\\",\\\"mocking async clients\\\",\\\"unit testing pipeline\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":1,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"Tests cover IntentClass types: EXECUTION, QUERY, and ESCALATION.\\\",\\\"Uses pytest and unittest.mock to simulate LiteLLM responses.\\\",\\\"Includes tests for handling ambiguous inputs that trigger ClarificationRequired exceptions.\\\",\\\"Mocks httpx.AsyncClient to control LLM response simulation.\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/tests/test_intent_interpreter.py\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8kh2v_cfafca65652b\\\",\\\"importance\\\":3,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Read the test suite for the intent interpreter to understand how the system handles different intent classifications and ambiguity levels. This provides context for the expected behavior of the LLM-driven intent parsing logic.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Examining unit tests for the IntentInterpreter pipeline component\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T17:59:54.486Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Read test_intent_interpreter.py\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_read\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"intent classification\\\",\\\"regex-based parsing\\\",\\\"hybrid retrieval\\\",\\\"entity extraction\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":1,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"The system uses a two-stage approach: regex-based pre-filtering followed by memory-based recall.\\\",\\\"Regex rules map specific command prefixes (e.g., 'list', 'show', 'deploy') to IntentClasses (QUERY, EXECUTION, etc.).\\\",\\\"The `_rule_classify` function provides 1.0 confidence/0.0 ambiguity for regex matches.\\\",\\\"`_extract_entity` parses input to identify target entities like models, services, or databases.\\\",\\\"`_recall_intent` queries 'intent-classifications' memory to find previously matched intents.\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8kk0g_72a49a3254a5\\\",\\\"importance\\\":5,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Inspected the core intent parsing logic in the pipeline. The implementation uses a hybrid approach of deterministic regex rules and a vector/memory search for historical intents.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Examining the rule-based and memory-based intent classification logic\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T17:59:58.286Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Read intent_interpreter.py implementation\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_read\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"prompt injection detection\\\",\\\"regex-based security scanning\\\",\\\"security auditing\\\",\\\"risk scoring\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":1,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"Uses regex patterns to detect common prompt injection strings (e.g., 'ignore previous instructions', 'DAN mode').\\\",\\\"Calculates a risk_score based on the proportion of matched patterns found.\\\",\\\"Integrates with EventLog to log security warnings when risk_score exceeds 0.1.\\\",\\\"Uses a dataclass InjectionResult to return scan results.\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/xnch/xnch/security/injection_guard.py\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8kqiz_7d454b6263ca\\\",\\\"importance\\\":4,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"The file contains the implementation for scanning text inputs for potential prompt injection attacks. It uses a predefined list of regex patterns to identify malicious instructions and logs attempts via an EventLog system.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Inspection of prompt injection detection logic\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T18:00:06.730Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Read security/injection_guard.py\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"file_read\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"unit testing\\\",\\\"intent classification\\\",\\\"mocking async methods\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":0.9,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"IntentInterpreter correctly mapped 'xyzzyplex frobnicate' to EXECUTION/DEPLOY intent class via mock\\\",\\\"Mocked _classify_with_llm was not called during the test execution\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8kzok_ec07fc0bf5c7\\\",\\\"importance\\\":5,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Executed a standalone Python script to verify if IntentInterpreter correctly processes input. The test showed the expected intent class and action type but revealed the LLM mock was not triggered as expected, suggesting a potential issue in the interpretation flow or method interception.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Running unit test for IntentInterpreter with mocked LLM\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-26T18:00:18.594Z\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Verify IntentInterpreter classification logic\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_run\\\"},\\\"type\\\":\\\"compressed\\\"},\\\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\\\":{\\\"observation\\\":{\\\"concepts\\\":[\\\"intent classification\\\",\\\"rule-based engine\\\",\\\"unit testing\\\",\\\"mocking\\\"],\\\"confidence\\\":1,\\\"facts\\\":[\\\"_rule_classify returned None for input 'xyzzyplex frobnicate'\\\",\\\"_recall_intent successfully identified an EXECUTION intent with DEPLOY action\\\",\\\"LLM classification was bypassed via mock, confirming-rule-based logic paths\\\"],\\\"files\\\":[\\\"/Users/xnch/xnchSystems/nexi/pipeline/intent_interpreter.py\\\"],\\\"id\\\":\\\"obs_mqv8l80m_9925f8563407\\\",\\\"importance\\\":5,\\\"narrative\\\":\\\"Ran a standalone Python test script to debug the internal components of IntentInterpreter. The test verified that rule-based classification failed for the dummy string, but the recall mechanism successfully identified a high-urgency deployment intent.\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"ses_0fb0da627ffe1MoEyui2GTY7HI\\\",\\\"subtitle\\\":\\\"Verifying rule-based classification and intent recall\\\",\\\"timestamp\